WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:32.676
Oh. we're screwed.
No more free Wi-Fi.

3
00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:35.012
- Hey. Ki-jung!
- Yeah?

4
00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:39.182
The lady upstairs
put a password on 'iptime'.

5
00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:41.018
A password?

6
00:01:41.143 --> 00:01:43.895
- Did you try 123456789?
- No luck.

7
00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:46.898
- Do it the other way.
- I tried that too.

8
00:01:47.024 --> 00:01:52.863
- Fuck. then we can't get WhatsApp?
- Nothing.

9
00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:55.032
Hey. Kim Ki-taek.

10
00:01:55.866 --> 00:01:59.036
Don't fucking pretend to sleep.
What do you think?

11
00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:05.334
Our phones are shut off.
Now our Wi-Fi is shut off.

12
00:02:06.168 --> 00:02:08.170
What's your plan?

13
00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:13.216
- Ki-woo.
- Yes. Dad?

14
00:02:13.342 --> 00:02:16.511
For Wi-Fi. hold it high.

15
00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.017
Stick it in every corner. and so on.

16
00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:29.650
Damn stink bugs.

17
00:02:30.442 --> 00:02:32.653
Over here! I got it!

18
00:02:32.778 --> 00:02:35.947
- Really? You got a signal?
- Yeah. see?

19
00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:38.742
This one. 'coffeeland 2G'.

20
00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:40.827
Did a new cafe open?

21
00:02:40.952 --> 00:02:44.206
- Why can't I get it?
- Climb up here.

22
00:02:44.331 --> 00:02:46.958
Hey. kids. Does it work?

23
00:02:47.084 --> 00:02:50.379
- (Ki-woo) Yeah.
- Then check WhatsApp.

24
00:02:51.046 --> 00:02:53.715
Pizza Generation
said they'd contact me.

25
00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.175
Hold on.

26
00:02:55.884 --> 00:02:58.011
Here it is. Pizza Generation.

27
00:03:01.348 --> 00:03:05.102
Wow! Check this out. guys.

28
00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:08.397
If we go as fast as her.
we can finish today.

29
00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:09.856
Then we can get paid.

30
00:03:09.981 --> 00:03:12.984
- Should we stand up too?
- (Chung-sook) She's a pro.

31
00:03:13.485 --> 00:03:16.154
What's that? Fumigation?

32
00:03:18.115 --> 00:03:20.659
- They still do that kind of thing?
- Guess so.

33
00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:22.452
- Shut the window.
- Leave it open.

34
00:03:22.577 --> 00:03:25.914
We'll get free extermination.
Kill the stink bugs.

35
00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.542
(Chung-sook)
Right. too many stink bugs these days.

36
00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:33.046
(Coughing) Oh. God. that smells!

37
00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:35.257
(Coughing and spluttering)

38
00:03:35.757 --> 00:03:39.761
- I told you to shut them!
- (Ki-woo) Should I shut them. Dad?

39
00:03:42.848 --> 00:03:45.225
(Coughing and spluttering)

40
00:03:50.647 --> 00:03:56.236
- What exactly is the problem?
- Take this one as an example.

41
00:03:56.361 --> 00:03:58.405
You call this a straight line?

42
00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.868
And why's it folded here?
Why is this sticking up?

43
00:04:02.993 --> 00:04:06.163
You didn't even fold it.

44
00:04:06.288 --> 00:04:10.375
A quarter of them look like this.

45
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.753
So 1 out of 4 are rejects.

46
00:04:16.423 --> 00:04:20.260
So you're really docking 10%
off our pay?

47
00:04:20.385 --> 00:04:23.805
Considering the rejects.
that's a low penalty. isn't it?

48
00:04:24.973 --> 00:04:27.768
Our pay is so low already!
How can you do this?

49
00:04:28.477 --> 00:04:29.895
(Sighs)

50
00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:34.107
Look here.
This is not some minor issue.

51
00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:39.654
You know what one shitty box
can do to our brand image?

52
00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.699
Brand? You can't even afford
a box folder!

53
00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:44.451
What did you say?

54
00:04:44.576 --> 00:04:46.578
(Laughs) Boss...

55
00:04:47.329 --> 00:04:49.748
- This is all because of that guy. right?
- What guy?

56
00:04:49.873 --> 00:04:53.710
Your part-time worker.
He's gone AWOL. right?

57
00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:57.798
Just when the Love of God Church
made a huge group order?

58
00:04:57.923 --> 00:05:00.175
How do you know all that?

59
00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.885
Who told you?

60
00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.970
My sister knows the guy.

61
00:05:04.095 --> 00:05:08.475
He's always been a bit strange.
Got a bad reputation.

62
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.977
Speaking of which. Boss.

63
00:05:11.102 --> 00:05:13.313
We'll accept a 10% penalty.

64
00:05:13.438 --> 00:05:15.774
- In return...
- In return?

65
00:05:15.899 --> 00:05:18.360
Any thought of hiring
a new part-time worker?

66
00:05:18.485 --> 00:05:22.405
Sis. we really need someone!

67
00:05:22.531 --> 00:05:26.076
Ditch the guy you've got now.
Just sack him.

68
00:05:26.201 --> 00:05:29.454
Tomorrow I'll come
for a formal interview. What time?

69
00:05:29.579 --> 00:05:31.248
Wait. hold on a sec.

70
00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.125
Let me think about it.

71
00:05:34.668 --> 00:05:37.963
Then. for now.
just pay for the boxes.

72
00:05:44.761 --> 00:05:47.931
So we're all gathered here today.

73
00:05:48.473 --> 00:05:51.852
to celebrate the reconnection
of our phones.

74
00:05:51.977 --> 00:05:55.772
and this bounteous Wi-Fi!

75
00:05:55.897 --> 00:05:59.150
Look at that bastard.
It's not even dark yet.

76
00:05:59.776 --> 00:06:04.364
Oh. why didn't you put up
a 'No Urinating' sign? I told you!

77
00:06:04.489 --> 00:06:08.577
No. signs like that just make them
piss even more.

78
00:06:09.828 --> 00:06:12.622
- At least shout at him!
- Don't shout.

79
00:06:13.081 --> 00:06:14.916
"Please don't piss!"

80
00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:19.504
(Ki-jung) Hey... is that Min?

81
00:06:20.255 --> 00:06:23.842
- (Min) Hey. mister. that's not a toilet!
- (Ki-jung) Way to go. Min.

82
00:06:23.967 --> 00:06:29.347
- (Drunk) Hey. punk!
- Who are you staring at. arsehole?

83
00:06:29.472 --> 00:06:32.684
(Drunk) Come here. you little shit.

84
00:06:34.603 --> 00:06:36.813
Get a fucking grip!

85
00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:40.150
Now. that's an impressive friend.

86
00:06:40.275 --> 00:06:43.278
College students
have a real vigour to them.

87
00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:44.613
Not like my brother.

88
00:06:44.738 --> 00:06:47.866
But is he coming here?
Did you invite him?

89
00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:49.034
No.

90
00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:51.620
- Hello!
- Oh. hi. Min.

91
00:06:52.245 --> 00:06:53.955
- Min!
- Are you well. sir?

92
00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.499
- Sure.
- What are you doing here?

93
00:06:56.625 --> 00:06:58.668
I texted you. Didn't you see it?

94
00:06:58.793 --> 00:07:01.296
- Sorry. were you eating?
- No. we weren't eating.

95
00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:03.715
- How are you. Ki-jung?
- Fine. You too?

96
00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.509
We could've met outside.
Why come here?

97
00:07:06.635 --> 00:07:10.305
Because of this.
It's for you. but it's so heavy.

98
00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.432
Really? Put it down here.

99
00:07:14.726 --> 00:07:16.353
Wow. what is that?

100
00:07:16.478 --> 00:07:21.024
(Min) When I said I was meeting Ki-woo.
my grandfather insisted I bring this.

101
00:07:25.695 --> 00:07:28.490
Ah... Is this a landscape type?

102
00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:31.117
Or you can see it as an abstract type.

103
00:07:31.242 --> 00:07:32.911
Wow. you know these!

104
00:07:33.036 --> 00:07:37.040
My grandpa has collected
scholar's rocks since his cadet days.

105
00:07:37.165 --> 00:07:40.627
Now the annex. the study.
every room in the house

106
00:07:40.752 --> 00:07:42.754
is filled with these things.

107
00:07:42.879 --> 00:07:46.675
But this stone here is said
to bring material wealth to families...

108
00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.388
Min... this is so metaphorical.

109
00:07:51.513 --> 00:07:55.600
- For sure. It's a very opportune gift.
- (Min) Of course.

110
00:07:55.725 --> 00:07:59.729
Please relay our deepest thanks
to your grandpa.

111
00:07:59.854 --> 00:08:01.731
Food would be better.

112
00:08:11.741 --> 00:08:16.579
What was that called? A landscape stone?
You collect those rocks too?

113
00:08:16.705 --> 00:08:20.875
Hey. thanks to that rock.
I saw your parents. they look healthy.

114
00:08:23.378 --> 00:08:27.007
They're plenty healthy. just out of work.

115
00:08:28.842 --> 00:08:31.136
Is Ki-jung taking lessons these days?

116
00:08:32.262 --> 00:08:35.098
She can't afford lessons.

117
00:08:44.024 --> 00:08:45.734
Cute. huh?

118
00:08:45.859 --> 00:08:48.778
She's the one you're tutoring?

119
00:08:48.903 --> 00:08:51.281
Park Da-hye. High school student.

120
00:08:51.406 --> 00:08:54.993
You take over as her English tutor.

121
00:08:55.118 --> 00:08:58.538
- What do you mean?
- Tutor a rich kid. It pays well.

122
00:08:59.581 --> 00:09:04.044
She's a nice girl. Look after her
while I'm studying abroad.

123
00:09:04.794 --> 00:09:08.173
What about your university friends?

124
00:09:08.298 --> 00:09:11.593
Why ask a loser like me?

125
00:09:12.135 --> 00:09:16.473
Why do you think?
Just the thought makes me sick.

126
00:09:16.598 --> 00:09:20.643
Those disgusting frat boys
slavering over Da-hye?

127
00:09:20.769 --> 00:09:22.771
It's revolting.

128
00:09:28.318 --> 00:09:29.861
You like her?

129
00:09:31.613 --> 00:09:33.907
(Laughter)

130
00:09:34.866 --> 00:09:37.077
Hey. I'm serious.

131
00:09:38.286 --> 00:09:41.915
When she enters university.
I'll officially ask her out.

132
00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:44.709
So you take care of her until then.

133
00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:48.338
If it's you. I can leave in peace.

134
00:09:50.465 --> 00:09:53.468
Thanks for your trust.

135
00:09:53.593 --> 00:09:57.180
but do I have to pretend to be
a college student?

136
00:09:58.765 --> 00:10:01.351
Ki-woo. think about it.

137
00:10:02.352 --> 00:10:05.897
For years.
including your military service.

138
00:10:06.022 --> 00:10:08.274
you took the university
entrance exam four times.

139
00:10:08.399 --> 00:10:11.986
Grammar. vocabulary.
composition. conversation...

140
00:10:12.112 --> 00:10:13.613
When it comes to English.

141
00:10:13.738 --> 00:10:17.617
you can teach ten times better
than those drunken college pricks.

142
00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:22.122
- I guess so.
- Sure!

143
00:10:22.247 --> 00:10:25.917
But will they hire me?
I'm not a college student.

144
00:10:26.042 --> 00:10:31.172
Just fake it. Don't worry.
you'll have my recommendation. plus...

145
00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:34.843
How should I describe the mother?

146
00:10:37.387 --> 00:10:40.181
She's a bit simple.
Young and simple.

147
00:10:40.306 --> 00:10:43.309
Simple? What do you mean?

148
00:10:43.434 --> 00:10:47.397
Anyway. it's all good.
I had fun there.

149
00:10:48.148 --> 00:10:50.817
- So you agree?
- I guess so.

150
00:10:52.193 --> 00:10:57.282
Hey. you said your sister's artistic?
Good at Photoshop?

151
00:11:00.451 --> 00:11:04.747
(Ki-woo) God. with skills like these.
why can't you get into art school?

152
00:11:04.873 --> 00:11:06.457
Shut up.

153
00:11:08.459 --> 00:11:10.587
Hey. it's no smoking in here.

154
00:11:10.712 --> 00:11:13.173
Yeah. yeah. Give me that.

155
00:11:17.218 --> 00:11:20.430
(Ki-woo) Oh. now the cherry on top.

156
00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:26.603
Wow. does Oxford have a degree
in document forgery?

157
00:11:26.728 --> 00:11:30.106
Ki-jung would be top of her class.

158
00:11:30.231 --> 00:11:32.901
(Ki-woo) She's amazing. huh?

159
00:11:33.026 --> 00:11:38.239
Our boy's going for a job interview.
Wish him luck.

160
00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:40.867
Son...

161
00:11:40.992 --> 00:11:43.745
I'm proud of you.

162
00:11:44.204 --> 00:11:49.375
Dad. I don't think of this
as forgery or crime.

163
00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.461
I'll go to this university next year.

164
00:11:51.586 --> 00:11:55.381
Oh... so you've got a plan.

165
00:11:55.506 --> 00:11:59.093
I just printed out the document
a bit early.

166
00:12:32.252 --> 00:12:34.003
(Bell rings)

167
00:12:34.504 --> 00:12:36.172
(Woman) 'Who is it?'

168
00:12:36.297 --> 00:12:40.051
Madame? Good afternoon.
I'm here on Min's recommendation...

169
00:12:40.176 --> 00:12:42.011
'Oh. right. come in.'

170
00:12:43.263 --> 00:12:44.472
Thank you.

171
00:12:45.431 --> 00:12:47.433
(Door locks buzz)

172
00:13:00.113 --> 00:13:01.531
(Door closes)

173
00:13:04.242 --> 00:13:05.660
(Bird song)

174
00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:18.256
(Woman) Hello!

175
00:13:18.381 --> 00:13:19.799
Hello. Madame.

176
00:13:19.924 --> 00:13:22.969
I just work here. Come this way.

177
00:13:23.761 --> 00:13:25.430
The yard is so nice.

178
00:13:25.555 --> 00:13:27.473
The inside's nice too.

179
00:13:27.598 --> 00:13:30.977
You know the architect Namgoong?
He's famous.

180
00:13:31.102 --> 00:13:33.521
He used to live in this house.

181
00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:37.942
He designed it himself.

182
00:13:40.945 --> 00:13:46.284
As you can see... now it's a playpen.

183
00:13:46.409 --> 00:13:47.827
This way.

184
00:13:49.912 --> 00:13:52.332
Sit yourself down here.
I'll bring the madame.

185
00:13:52.457 --> 00:13:53.791
Yes.

186
00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.347
(Woman) Madame.

187
00:14:07.972 --> 00:14:09.307
Madame?

188
00:14:11.851 --> 00:14:13.227
Madame?

189
00:14:14.979 --> 00:14:16.397
Madame?

190
00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:22.195
He's here. The tutoring candidate.

191
00:14:25.865 --> 00:14:28.451
I don't care about documents.

192
00:14:28.576 --> 00:14:31.204
Min recommended you. after all.

193
00:14:31.996 --> 00:14:37.752
As you know.
Min is such a brilliant human being.

194
00:14:38.628 --> 00:14:40.797
Da-hye and I were quite happy with him.

195
00:14:40.922 --> 00:14:44.175
Regardless of her grades.
Know what I mean?

196
00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:45.635
Yes.

197
00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.512
Oh. he was marvellous.

198
00:14:47.637 --> 00:14:54.602
So to be honest. we wanted to stick
with him through high school.

199
00:14:55.645 --> 00:14:58.481
But all of a sudden. he's going abroad.

200
00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:06.406
Anyway. excuse me.
but if I can speak directly...

201
00:15:06.531 --> 00:15:11.327
If you're not up to Min's level.

202
00:15:11.452 --> 00:15:13.871
then I'm not sure what the point is.

203
00:15:15.665 --> 00:15:19.585
So anyway.
what I want to say is.

204
00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:24.757
for your first lesson today.
do you mind if I sit in?

205
00:15:25.508 --> 00:15:29.137
I want to see how you run your lesson.

206
00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:33.307
(Speaks English) Is it okay with you?

207
00:15:39.605 --> 00:15:40.940
(Dog barks)

208
00:16:01.711 --> 00:16:04.338
You sure about ♪24?

209
00:16:11.262 --> 00:16:16.184
Da-hye. you solved those later problems
then went back to ♪24.

210
00:16:16.309 --> 00:16:17.727
Right?

211
00:16:19.353 --> 00:16:20.688
Yes.

212
00:16:22.899 --> 00:16:23.941
(Da-hye gasps)

213
00:16:28.488 --> 00:16:33.659
If that were the first question
on a real exam. you'd be screwed.

214
00:16:34.327 --> 00:16:37.455
Look. your pulse is racing.

215
00:16:40.458 --> 00:16:43.461
The heart doesn't lie.

216
00:16:44.754 --> 00:16:48.174
An exam is like
slashing through a jungle.

217
00:16:48.299 --> 00:16:51.219
Lose that momentum
and you're finished.

218
00:16:51.344 --> 00:16:53.638
The answer to ♪24?
I don't care.

219
00:16:53.763 --> 00:16:59.393
Slashing through the exam.
dominating it.

220
00:16:59.519 --> 00:17:01.354
that's all I care about.

221
00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:05.691
What you need is vigour.

222
00:17:07.401 --> 00:17:08.819
Vigour.

223
00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:11.447
Understand?

224
00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:25.044
(Yeon-kyo) So I'll pay you this time
each month.

225
00:17:25.169 --> 00:17:28.172
Three classes a week.
two hours each. okay?

226
00:17:28.965 --> 00:17:30.383
As for the fee.

227
00:17:30.508 --> 00:17:34.095
I was going to pay Min's rate.
then I added a bit for inflation.

228
00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:35.638
Thank you.

229
00:17:37.223 --> 00:17:39.225
How about a proper introduction?

230
00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:41.936
Da-hye's tutor. we'll call him Kevin.

231
00:17:42.895 --> 00:17:44.939
Mr. Kevin!

232
00:17:45.064 --> 00:17:48.526
If you feel like snacking
during your lesson. just call me.

233
00:17:48.651 --> 00:17:50.695
If you need anything. ask her.

234
00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:53.030
She knows this house better than I...

235
00:17:53.155 --> 00:17:56.784
(Gasps)
Da-song. stop it!

236
00:17:56.909 --> 00:17:58.911
- (Ki-woo laughs)
- I'm sorry. did he startle you?

237
00:17:59.036 --> 00:18:01.330
How cute. His name's Da-song?

238
00:18:01.455 --> 00:18:03.249
Yes. our youngest.

239
00:18:03.374 --> 00:18:06.419
Da-song. come and say hi!
This is Mr. Kevin!

240
00:18:08.879 --> 00:18:13.301
This is an Indian arrow.
I ordered it from the US.

241
00:18:13.426 --> 00:18:18.264
From last year
he's been an Indian fanatic. Ah...

242
00:18:18.389 --> 00:18:23.102
Indians?
He's got a fanboy personality?

243
00:18:23.227 --> 00:18:26.772
Well. he's eccentric
and easily distracted.

244
00:18:26.897 --> 00:18:29.734
he can barely sit still.

245
00:18:29.859 --> 00:18:31.986
So last year I enrolled him
in the Cub Scouts.

246
00:18:32.111 --> 00:18:35.031
hoping he'd learn moderation and focus.

247
00:18:35.156 --> 00:18:38.618
But look... he's even worse.

248
00:18:41.412 --> 00:18:46.250
His scout leader is an Indian fanatic.
maybe that's why.

249
00:18:46.917 --> 00:18:51.297
The American Indian is
the very spirit of the Cub Scouts.

250
00:18:51.422 --> 00:18:55.551
- It's a good thing.
- Were you a Cub Scout. Kevin?

251
00:18:55.676 --> 00:18:58.971
Sure. I'm a Scout by nature.

252
00:18:59.096 --> 00:19:03.017
(Yeon-kyo) Da-song is an artist by nature.
Look at this painting.

253
00:19:04.185 --> 00:19:07.104
It's so metaphorical. Really strong.

254
00:19:07.229 --> 00:19:08.856
Strong. right?

255
00:19:08.981 --> 00:19:11.108
You've got an eye for this.

256
00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.111
It's a chimpanzee. right?

257
00:19:14.236 --> 00:19:15.863
A self-portrait.

258
00:19:18.699 --> 00:19:20.201
Sure enough!

259
00:19:21.369 --> 00:19:24.830
The perspective of a young artist
eludes understanding.

260
00:19:24.955 --> 00:19:27.500
Or perhaps it's Da-song's
expressive genius...

261
00:19:27.625 --> 00:19:32.922
Anyway. we've been through
so many art teachers.

262
00:19:33.047 --> 00:19:35.007
None of them lasts even a month.

263
00:19:37.051 --> 00:19:39.679
And Da-song is just so hard to control.

264
00:19:42.515 --> 00:19:45.309
- Just a moment. Madame.
- Yes?

265
00:19:45.434 --> 00:19:50.856
Someone just came to mind.
What was her name?

266
00:19:50.981 --> 00:19:53.901
Jessica! Right. Jessica...

267
00:19:54.026 --> 00:19:58.030
She was in the same art school
as my cousin.

268
00:19:58.489 --> 00:20:00.991
What was her Korean name?

269
00:20:01.117 --> 00:20:06.122
Anyway. after studying applied arts
at Illinois State University.

270
00:20:06.247 --> 00:20:08.040
she returned to Korea.

271
00:20:08.165 --> 00:20:10.876
Illinois... Tell me more.

272
00:20:11.001 --> 00:20:16.549
Her teaching is unusual.
but she knows how to handle kids.

273
00:20:17.633 --> 00:20:20.761
She's got a special reputation
in her field.

274
00:20:20.886 --> 00:20:23.264
But even though
her methods are unique.

275
00:20:23.389 --> 00:20:25.683
she can help kids
get into good art schools.

276
00:20:25.808 --> 00:20:30.146
Now I'm really curious. What's she like?

277
00:20:30.271 --> 00:20:32.064
Would you like to meet her?

278
00:20:32.189 --> 00:20:35.151
I heard. though.
she's in high demand...

279
00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:43.242
Hold on.

280
00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:47.663
♪ Jessica. only child.
Illinois. Chicago

281
00:20:47.788 --> 00:20:50.791
♪ Classmate Kim Jin-mo.
He's your cousin ♪

282
00:20:57.965 --> 00:21:01.886
(Yeon-kyo) Look at how he painted
the side dishes on the tablecloth

283
00:21:02.011 --> 00:21:04.346
in this mosaic arrangement.

284
00:21:04.472 --> 00:21:07.141
But within that too.
there are repeating patterns.

285
00:21:07.266 --> 00:21:09.935
Gochujang sauce is red. the rice...

286
00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:16.108
Well. anyway. he has a Basquiat-esque
sense even at the age of 9!

287
00:21:16.233 --> 00:21:17.777
How exciting.

288
00:21:17.902 --> 00:21:23.240
I'm sure Miss Jessica
must have already sensed this.

289
00:21:23.365 --> 00:21:27.912
so I'll leave you two
and go up for Da-hye's lesson.

290
00:21:28.037 --> 00:21:31.665
- Have a nice lesson. Jessica.
- Yes. thank you for the introduction.

291
00:21:35.544 --> 00:21:40.758
So. as you can see.
Da-song's eccentric genius...

292
00:21:43.511 --> 00:21:48.098
Da-hye...
So we'll start with ♪38?

293
00:21:52.686 --> 00:21:55.272
- Mr. Kevin?
- Hmm?

294
00:21:55.397 --> 00:22:00.361
Did you know that
Da-song is faking it all?

295
00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:03.364
Huh? What do you mean?

296
00:22:03.489 --> 00:22:05.157
It's all a show.

297
00:22:05.282 --> 00:22:08.994
Acting like a genius.
that 4th dimension stuff. it's all fake.

298
00:22:09.119 --> 00:22:12.248
- An artist cosplay.
- Da-song?

299
00:22:13.874 --> 00:22:15.501
You know that thing.

300
00:22:15.626 --> 00:22:20.256
when he freezes and stares at the sky
as if struck by inspiration.

301
00:22:20.381 --> 00:22:26.387
So he's walking along. then he stares
at the clouds for 10 minutes.

302
00:22:26.512 --> 00:22:30.975
So you know what I mean?
He gives me the creeps!

303
00:22:31.100 --> 00:22:34.728
He pretends that
he can't live a normal life.

304
00:22:34.854 --> 00:22:37.857
- Makes me want to puke.
- Hmm...

305
00:22:37.982 --> 00:22:40.150
So Da-song is pretending...

306
00:22:40.276 --> 00:22:44.113
But what's that got to do
with your studies?

307
00:22:48.117 --> 00:22:51.829
Well... I'm just saying...

308
00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:56.292
Sure. so in that sense...

309
00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:02.214
what you told me about Da-song
was very interesting.

310
00:23:02.339 --> 00:23:04.383
so let's write about it in English.

311
00:23:04.508 --> 00:23:10.306
And be sure to use the word 'pretend'
at least twice.

312
00:23:11.098 --> 00:23:14.059
Then. can I ask you a question?

313
00:23:15.352 --> 00:23:17.521
That teacher Jessica...

314
00:23:18.731 --> 00:23:24.612
Is she really your cousin's classmate?

315
00:23:26.864 --> 00:23:28.574
What do you mean?

316
00:23:28.699 --> 00:23:30.784
She's your girlfriend. right?

317
00:23:34.455 --> 00:23:37.917
No way! I just met her today.

318
00:23:42.004 --> 00:23:44.965
Jessica's really pretty. isn't she?

319
00:23:45.758 --> 00:23:47.635
Aren't you interested?

320
00:23:49.470 --> 00:23:51.597
You saw her?

321
00:23:51.722 --> 00:23:55.100
Sure. she's pretty.
She's a beautiful woman.

322
00:23:55.225 --> 00:23:56.560
Yeah.

323
00:23:58.437 --> 00:24:01.398
I knew it.

324
00:24:02.191 --> 00:24:04.193
So you are interested.

325
00:24:06.987 --> 00:24:08.405
Da-hye...

326
00:24:10.824 --> 00:24:17.498
So... if we can compare Jessica
to a rose.

327
00:24:17.623 --> 00:24:19.625
then you are...

328
00:25:05.212 --> 00:25:06.839
- Let's study.
- Yes.

329
00:25:06.964 --> 00:25:12.094
Please understand that
my boy has trouble keeping still.

330
00:25:12.219 --> 00:25:15.055
- I understand.
- Da-song!

331
00:25:16.473 --> 00:25:18.600
Da-song. get up!
Come on. Da-song!

332
00:25:19.226 --> 00:25:20.811
In your butt...

333
00:25:20.936 --> 00:25:23.814
- Madame. please leave us.
- What?

334
00:25:23.939 --> 00:25:26.692
I never teach with a parent in the room.

335
00:25:26.817 --> 00:25:29.111
But today is our first day.
and as you can see. he's...

336
00:25:29.236 --> 00:25:31.071
Wait downstairs.

337
00:25:32.406 --> 00:25:34.742
- Park Da-song?
- (Yeon-kyo) Da-song!

338
00:25:39.079 --> 00:25:41.373
- (Housekeeper) Madame?
- Hmm?

339
00:25:41.498 --> 00:25:44.043
- Want some plum extract?
- What?

340
00:25:44.168 --> 00:25:47.337
It's mixed with honey.
To ease your tension.

341
00:25:47.463 --> 00:25:49.715
Yeah. that would be great.

342
00:26:04.396 --> 00:26:06.523
- (Yeon-kyo) Hey.
- Yes?

343
00:26:06.648 --> 00:26:11.403
I've got an idea. Take two glasses
of plum extract to Da-song's room.

344
00:26:11.528 --> 00:26:14.448
You're not a parent.
so you can go in.

345
00:26:14.573 --> 00:26:16.033
Oh. that's right.

346
00:26:16.158 --> 00:26:18.994
Then I'll report back
on what's going on in there.

347
00:26:19.995 --> 00:26:21.789
Why didn't I think of it earlier?

348
00:26:24.249 --> 00:26:28.212
- What? They came out?
- (Housekeeper) Yeah.

349
00:26:30.756 --> 00:26:33.467
So you're done already?

350
00:26:35.177 --> 00:26:38.806
Madame. come and sit next to me.

351
00:26:41.141 --> 00:26:45.562
- Da-song. go upstairs.
- (Yeon-kyo) Hurry up!

352
00:26:52.694 --> 00:26:55.656
- Da-song just painted this.
- I see...

353
00:26:57.574 --> 00:26:59.993
I'd rather speak with Madame alone.

354
00:27:00.119 --> 00:27:04.039
- Oh. but she's...
- No. leave us.

355
00:27:08.627 --> 00:27:14.758
Madame. I told you that I study
art psychology and art therapy.

356
00:27:14.883 --> 00:27:16.593
Yes.

357
00:27:16.718 --> 00:27:19.138
Did anything happen to Da-song
in first year?

358
00:27:19.263 --> 00:27:20.889
(Gasps)

359
00:27:22.933 --> 00:27:27.938
To be frank. before I decide
whether to take on Da-song.

360
00:27:28.063 --> 00:27:30.858
I need to hear about this.

361
00:27:30.983 --> 00:27:34.945
But this is hard for me
to talk about right now.

362
00:27:35.070 --> 00:27:38.031
- What to do?
- Never mind. then.

363
00:27:38.157 --> 00:27:43.120
The lower-right region of a painting
is called the 'schizophrenia zone'.

364
00:27:43.245 --> 00:27:45.664
Psychotic symptoms
often reveal themselves here.

365
00:27:45.789 --> 00:27:47.749
- Oh. phrenia...
- And look here.

366
00:27:47.875 --> 00:27:50.419
Da-song painted
this unusual shape. right?

367
00:27:50.544 --> 00:27:51.837
I see.

368
00:27:54.214 --> 00:27:56.717
Over there. it's the same!
It's the same. right?

369
00:27:56.842 --> 00:27:59.052
Yes. that's correct.

370
00:27:59.178 --> 00:28:02.723
A similar shape in the same zone.
You see it now?

371
00:28:02.848 --> 00:28:08.979
Yes. I've stared
at that painting at every meal!

372
00:28:09.104 --> 00:28:11.231
But I had no idea.

373
00:28:11.356 --> 00:28:14.193
Calm down.
Let's compose ourselves.

374
00:28:14.902 --> 00:28:18.405
This is all a black box
into Da-song's mind.

375
00:28:18.530 --> 00:28:22.034
Would you like to open
that box with me. Madame?

376
00:28:23.035 --> 00:28:24.536
I want to open it.

377
00:28:24.661 --> 00:28:29.082
Then we'll need four
two-hour sessions per week.

378
00:28:29.208 --> 00:28:33.545
and this is not simple tutoring.
it's art therapy. right?

379
00:28:33.670 --> 00:28:34.838
Of course.

380
00:28:34.963 --> 00:28:39.009
Because of that.
my rate is set at a very high level.

381
00:28:39.134 --> 00:28:41.553
- Are you okay with that?
- It's my pleasure.

382
00:28:42.137 --> 00:28:45.015
- (Alarm pad beeps)
- Da-song's father is home.

383
00:28:45.140 --> 00:28:46.558
(Clears throat)

384
00:28:51.396 --> 00:28:55.442
Honey. Da-song's
new art teacher is here.

385
00:28:58.237 --> 00:29:00.280
Her name's Jessica. from Illinois.

386
00:29:00.989 --> 00:29:02.908
(Speaks English)
Jessica! This is Dong-ik.

387
00:29:03.033 --> 00:29:07.162
- Hello.
- Hi. Thanks for your help.

388
00:29:07.287 --> 00:29:09.623
- Is the class over?
- Yes. just finished.

389
00:29:09.748 --> 00:29:11.291
- Driver Yoon...
- Yes. sir?

390
00:29:11.416 --> 00:29:12.876
- Are you free?
- I am. sir.

391
00:29:13.001 --> 00:29:15.545
Then give her a lift. okay?

392
00:29:15.671 --> 00:29:20.133
Sure. we don't want her going down
alone at night. right?

393
00:29:20.259 --> 00:29:21.802
(Yoon) Of course.

394
00:29:21.927 --> 00:29:28.558
Miss Jessica? Shall I drive you
all the way home. then?

395
00:29:29.893 --> 00:29:32.562
- Which neighbourhood...?
- No. that's fine.

396
00:29:32.688 --> 00:29:36.566
You can just drop me off
at Hyehwa station.

397
00:29:36.692 --> 00:29:38.944
- Thank you.
- I don't mind if it's far.

398
00:29:39.069 --> 00:29:42.990
- My shift's finished. anyway.
- I'll get out at Hyehwa.

399
00:29:43.115 --> 00:29:46.243
Looks like it's going to rain.

400
00:29:48.078 --> 00:29:50.580
Ride the Benz. not the subway!

401
00:29:50.706 --> 00:29:54.251
I'm meeting my boyfriend
at exit 3 of Hyehwa Station!

402
00:29:55.294 --> 00:29:56.712
Yes.

403
00:30:17.691 --> 00:30:19.526
(Angry shouting)

404
00:30:31.246 --> 00:30:34.958
Dad. when you worked as a driver.
did you drive a lot of Benzes?

405
00:30:35.667 --> 00:30:42.549
Benzes? Not then.
but I did when I worked as a valet.

406
00:30:42.674 --> 00:30:45.302
Ah... you worked as a valet?

407
00:30:45.427 --> 00:30:49.014
Sure. after the chicken place went bust.
before the Taiwan cake shop.

408
00:30:49.139 --> 00:30:50.974
in that six-month window?

409
00:30:51.099 --> 00:30:54.561
No. it was after
the cake shop went bust.

410
00:30:57.481 --> 00:31:00.067
We're moving to the next stage already?

411
00:31:00.192 --> 00:31:03.737
(Ki-jung) I set a trap in the Benz.

412
00:31:03.862 --> 00:31:08.200
Then we're diving right in.
Wow. this is so metaphorical.

413
00:31:08.325 --> 00:31:11.787
Look. Dad. we're eating
in a driver's cafeteria right now.

414
00:31:12.496 --> 00:31:14.831
Right. a driver's cafeteria!

415
00:31:14.956 --> 00:31:17.084
Eat as much as you want. kids.

416
00:31:17.209 --> 00:31:19.753
You didn't even pay for it.
they did!

417
00:31:19.878 --> 00:31:23.131
Son. have some more. Eat up!

418
00:31:23.256 --> 00:31:25.258
- Yes. Dad.
- Eat your fill.

419
00:31:25.384 --> 00:31:27.427
What did you do
to that woman yesterday?

420
00:31:27.552 --> 00:31:30.055
- What?
- She was freaking out.

421
00:31:30.180 --> 00:31:32.516
Saying she was so moved.
you put her in shock.

422
00:31:32.641 --> 00:31:38.146
Fuck. I don't know! I googled
'art therapy'. and ad-libbed the rest.

423
00:31:38.271 --> 00:31:40.690
Then suddenly. she's weeping.

424
00:31:40.816 --> 00:31:42.818
Crazy bitch. I couldn't believe it.

425
00:32:16.268 --> 00:32:18.645
Oh. you're home?

426
00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:20.564
Have you eaten yet?

427
00:32:22.315 --> 00:32:23.817
Is something wrong?

428
00:32:23.942 --> 00:32:27.028
- Is the housekeeper out?
- She's walking the dogs.

429
00:32:27.904 --> 00:32:29.322
Honey...

430
00:32:30.240 --> 00:32:32.325
This was under my car seat.

431
00:32:34.828 --> 00:32:36.955
Driver Yoon is such a scumbag.

432
00:32:37.080 --> 00:32:38.540
What is this?

433
00:32:39.541 --> 00:32:43.295
I'm sorry. honey.
I didn't know he was that kind of guy.

434
00:32:43.420 --> 00:32:46.173
Don't you pay him well?

435
00:32:46.798 --> 00:32:49.968
Is he saving up
by not paying for a hotel room?

436
00:32:50.093 --> 00:32:52.888
He must be a pervert.
He likes it in the car.

437
00:32:53.013 --> 00:32:57.058
Oh. that's gross. In his boss' car!

438
00:32:57.184 --> 00:33:01.396
A young guy's sex life is
his own business. that's all fine.

439
00:33:05.275 --> 00:33:07.444
But why in my car?

440
00:33:08.904 --> 00:33:12.741
And if so. why not in his seat?
Why cross the line like that?

441
00:33:12.866 --> 00:33:14.534
You're right.

442
00:33:14.659 --> 00:33:17.829
Does dripping his sperm on my seat
turn him on?

443
00:33:17.954 --> 00:33:19.831
I can't believe this.

444
00:33:24.586 --> 00:33:28.590
But you know
what's strangest of all?

445
00:33:29.549 --> 00:33:31.551
What?

446
00:33:31.676 --> 00:33:34.054
Usually. if you have car sex.

447
00:33:34.179 --> 00:33:39.476
you might leave behind
a strand of hair or an earring.

448
00:33:39.601 --> 00:33:40.769
Right.

449
00:33:40.894 --> 00:33:44.773
But how can you forget
your own panties?

450
00:33:44.898 --> 00:33:48.777
That's right. Hard to overlook.

451
00:33:49.986 --> 00:33:53.823
So it makes me quite suspicious
of this woman's condition.

452
00:33:55.116 --> 00:33:56.660
You get me?

453
00:34:01.498 --> 00:34:02.916
(Whispers)

454
00:34:06.169 --> 00:34:09.881
- Oh. my Meth or cocaine?
- Shh! The kids...

455
00:34:10.006 --> 00:34:14.010
What do we do? What if anyone finds
white powder in your car?

456
00:34:14.135 --> 00:34:16.471
Calm down. relax.

457
00:34:17.264 --> 00:34:19.057
Relax...

458
00:34:19.182 --> 00:34:22.936
For now. it's just supposition.
A rational guess.

459
00:34:23.061 --> 00:34:26.523
- But no need to call the police.
- Not that!

460
00:34:27.607 --> 00:34:33.071
Still. for a busy man like me to ask.
"Why are you fucking in my car?"

461
00:34:33.196 --> 00:34:36.449
- (Yeon-kyo) Exactly.
- So instead...

462
00:34:36.575 --> 00:34:41.371
...can you just invent
some bland excuse to let him go?

463
00:34:41.496 --> 00:34:42.914
Okay. sure.

464
00:34:43.039 --> 00:34:46.042
No need to mention panties or car sex.

465
00:34:46.167 --> 00:34:48.545
We don't need to stoop
to that level. do we?

466
00:34:48.670 --> 00:34:50.171
Surely not!

467
00:34:50.797 --> 00:34:53.842
But what if he goes online
and accuses us...

468
00:34:53.967 --> 00:34:56.511
- Just give him a good severance.
- Oh!

469
00:34:56.636 --> 00:34:59.764
How was Da-song today?

470
00:34:59.889 --> 00:35:01.891
(Ki-jung) He was fine.

471
00:35:02.684 --> 00:35:04.644
- So class is finished?
- Yes.

472
00:35:04.769 --> 00:35:09.816
Jessica. the last time you came.
our driver gave you a ride. right?

473
00:35:09.941 --> 00:35:11.276
That's right.

474
00:35:11.401 --> 00:35:15.071
This may be an odd question.
but nothing happened then?

475
00:35:15.196 --> 00:35:16.906
No. he was very nice.

476
00:35:17.032 --> 00:35:22.037
I told him to go to Hyehwa Station.
but he insisted on driving me home.

477
00:35:22.162 --> 00:35:25.332
That idiot!
He took you home late at night?

478
00:35:25.457 --> 00:35:30.420
- Revealing where you live?
- No. I got off at Hyehwa.

479
00:35:30.545 --> 00:35:34.716
Oh. good girl. Very good.
Jessica. nice...

480
00:35:34.841 --> 00:35:36.968
Did something happen with him?

481
00:35:37.093 --> 00:35:42.307
He won't be working for us anymore.
A slightly shameful incident.

482
00:35:42.432 --> 00:35:44.351
What incident?

483
00:35:44.476 --> 00:35:47.103
Oh. you don't need to know.

484
00:35:48.730 --> 00:35:52.567
But I'm surprised.
He was so gentlemanly and cool.

485
00:35:52.692 --> 00:35:56.196
Jessica. you're too young and innocent!

486
00:35:56.321 --> 00:35:58.865
- You have a lot to learn about people.
- (Dogs barking)

487
00:35:58.990 --> 00:36:03.787
But we were excited to have
such a young. hip driver. too.

488
00:36:03.912 --> 00:36:07.040
But isn't an older driver better?

489
00:36:07.165 --> 00:36:11.127
That's true. They drive better.
have better manners.

490
00:36:11.252 --> 00:36:13.880
My father's brother had a driver
just like that.

491
00:36:14.005 --> 00:36:18.593
Mr. Kim.
He was so congenial and nice.

492
00:36:18.718 --> 00:36:21.054
I used to call him Uncle
when I was young.

493
00:36:21.179 --> 00:36:23.139
You know a man like that?

494
00:36:23.264 --> 00:36:26.017
Yes. he was so mild-mannered.

495
00:36:27.102 --> 00:36:31.314
Oh. but my relatives relocated
to Chicago.

496
00:36:32.732 --> 00:36:34.818
I wonder if Mr. Kim's free now?

497
00:36:35.735 --> 00:36:39.280
I'm really interested.
Could I meet him?

498
00:36:39.406 --> 00:36:42.325
- Really?
- I don't trust anyone now.

499
00:36:43.201 --> 00:36:46.371
I only trust people recommended
by someone I know well.

500
00:36:46.496 --> 00:36:50.625
But if you've known him so long.
I'd feel much more at ease.

501
00:36:53.670 --> 00:36:56.005
Do you really want to meet him?

502
00:36:56.131 --> 00:36:57.924
(Speaks English)
I'm deadly serious.

503
00:36:58.049 --> 00:37:01.803
This chain of recommendations is best.

504
00:37:01.928 --> 00:37:05.223
How should I describe it?
A belt of trust?

505
00:37:05.348 --> 00:37:07.350
- This one's different.
- Here.

506
00:37:07.475 --> 00:37:10.603
Oh. right. And this one.
Looks like a touch screen now.

507
00:37:10.729 --> 00:37:13.523
It's not touch.
it says you have to turn it.

508
00:37:13.648 --> 00:37:15.358
Wow. this thing?

509
00:37:16.025 --> 00:37:19.195
Sir? Taking our time. are we?

510
00:37:22.365 --> 00:37:24.284
This is a nice car.

511
00:37:26.286 --> 00:37:28.371
This is it! Come over here.

512
00:37:31.833 --> 00:37:33.960
He's in a meeting now.

513
00:37:38.381 --> 00:37:40.842
Have a seat and wait here.

514
00:37:49.017 --> 00:37:52.187
Hello. nice to meet...

515
00:37:52.312 --> 00:37:53.730
(inaudible)

516
00:37:55.648 --> 00:37:57.066
But is it compatible with a phone?

517
00:37:57.192 --> 00:38:03.615
(Man) Oh. not with a phone.
You need more computing power.

518
00:38:05.241 --> 00:38:09.329
This isn't any sort of test.
so don't be nervous.

519
00:38:10.580 --> 00:38:13.124
I was worn out at the office.
so I came out for a bit.

520
00:38:13.249 --> 00:38:15.293
I understand.

521
00:38:15.418 --> 00:38:20.048
Constant chatter. all that bother.
At least the car is peaceful.

522
00:38:20.173 --> 00:38:23.676
- (Switches off sat-nav)
- Oh. thank you.

523
00:38:24.427 --> 00:38:29.307
- You seem to know the roads well?
- Anywhere below the 38th parallel.

524
00:38:29.432 --> 00:38:32.393
After 30 years behind the wheel.
the car almost drives itself.

525
00:38:32.519 --> 00:38:36.022
I respect those who work
in one field for a long time.

526
00:38:36.147 --> 00:38:39.150
Well. to be honest.
this is a simple vocation.

527
00:38:39.275 --> 00:38:44.280
But... the head of a household.
the leader of a company?

528
00:38:44.405 --> 00:38:49.202
Or else just a lonely man setting off
on the road each morning...

529
00:38:49.994 --> 00:38:52.247
It's companionship of a sort.

530
00:38:52.372 --> 00:38:55.166
so that's how I've approached each day.

531
00:38:55.291 --> 00:38:57.335
The years sure pass quickly.

532
00:39:00.922 --> 00:39:03.216
Sure enough.
your cornering is excellent.

533
00:39:04.551 --> 00:39:10.473
Well. it may look simple.
but it's one of the fundamentals.

534
00:39:10.598 --> 00:39:15.436
(Ki-jung) 'She may look like a sheep.
but inside she's a fox.

535
00:39:15.562 --> 00:39:18.898
'Sometimes she acts
like she owns the house.'

536
00:39:19.023 --> 00:39:22.694
(Ki-woo) 'Right.
Of all the people in that house.

537
00:39:22.819 --> 00:39:24.779
'she's lived there the longest.

538
00:39:24.904 --> 00:39:28.491
'She was housekeeper
to the architect Namgoong.

539
00:39:28.616 --> 00:39:33.371
'but then she went on
to work for this family.

540
00:39:33.496 --> 00:39:35.164
'When the architect moved out.

541
00:39:35.290 --> 00:39:38.167
'he introduced this woman
to Park's family.

542
00:39:38.293 --> 00:39:41.713
'telling them. "This is a great
housekeeper. you should hire her."'

543
00:39:41.838 --> 00:39:45.174
(Ki-jung) 'So she survived
change of ownership.'

544
00:39:45.300 --> 00:39:48.303
She won't give up a good job easily.

545
00:39:48.428 --> 00:39:51.598
To extract a woman like that.
we need to prepare well.

546
00:39:53.266 --> 00:39:55.643
Right. we need a plan.

547
00:39:57.061 --> 00:40:00.440
I want to eat peaches.
I like peaches best.

548
00:40:00.565 --> 00:40:02.025
Why not ask for some?

549
00:40:02.150 --> 00:40:05.737
No peaches at our house.
It's forbidden fruit.

550
00:40:13.703 --> 00:40:16.539
(Ki-woo) 'So according
to what Da-hye told me.

551
00:40:16.664 --> 00:40:21.252
'she's got a massively serious
allergy to peaches.

552
00:40:21.377 --> 00:40:24.172
'You know that fuzz on a peach's skin?

553
00:40:24.714 --> 00:40:28.301
'If she's anywhere near it.
she gets a full body rash.

554
00:40:28.426 --> 00:40:32.138
'has trouble breathing.
asthma. a total meltdown!'

555
00:40:33.890 --> 00:40:36.893
(Violent coughing and choking)

556
00:40:37.018 --> 00:40:40.772
No. no. there weren't
any peaches anywhere.

557
00:40:42.732 --> 00:40:45.401
That's what I'm saying!

558
00:40:45.526 --> 00:40:47.946
Usually when I get symptoms like this.

559
00:40:48.071 --> 00:40:51.407
I run to my room and take my medicine.

560
00:40:51.532 --> 00:40:57.163
but it was so sudden.
I wasn't sure where I left it.

561
00:40:57.288 --> 00:41:02.043
Madame. this woman behind me.
is that...?

562
00:41:02.168 --> 00:41:04.087
Oh. it's our housekeeper.

563
00:41:04.212 --> 00:41:06.798
So it's true. Oh. how sad.

564
00:41:06.923 --> 00:41:09.884
I wasn't sure if that was really her.

565
00:41:10.009 --> 00:41:13.429
I've only seen her a couple times
in the living room.

566
00:41:14.263 --> 00:41:16.140
This was in the hospital?

567
00:41:16.265 --> 00:41:20.520
A few days ago. I went
for my annual medical exam.

568
00:41:20.645 --> 00:41:25.149
I took a selfie for my wife.
and there she was. behind me.

569
00:41:25.274 --> 00:41:27.402
Is she talking on the phone there?

570
00:41:27.527 --> 00:41:31.072
Anyway. I wasn't trying to eavesdrop...

571
00:41:31.197 --> 00:41:34.575
I wasn't trying to eavesdrop.
but her words came through clearly!

572
00:41:34.701 --> 00:41:36.452
- So I couldn't help but...!
- Cut!

573
00:41:36.577 --> 00:41:41.457
Dad. your emotions are up to here.
Bring them down to about there.

574
00:41:42.125 --> 00:41:44.711
...so I couldn't help but overhear.

575
00:41:44.836 --> 00:41:47.338
Keep it focused!

576
00:41:48.965 --> 00:41:52.802
What I'm trying to say is.
it's just that.

577
00:41:52.927 --> 00:41:55.847
your housekeeper's voice
is quite loud. you know?

578
00:41:55.972 --> 00:41:59.892
I understand. it's all right.
Just tell me. okay?

579
00:42:00.018 --> 00:42:02.311
She said she'd been diagnosed
with active TB.

580
00:42:02.437 --> 00:42:04.480
and she was shouting on the phone.

581
00:42:04.605 --> 00:42:07.817
so upset. she could barely
control herself!

582
00:42:07.942 --> 00:42:10.111
Tuberculosis? Come on...

583
00:42:10.236 --> 00:42:15.742
It's true. she phoned someone
saying she had active TB.

584
00:42:15.867 --> 00:42:17.994
Do people still get TB?

585
00:42:18.119 --> 00:42:20.538
Do people still get TB?

586
00:42:20.663 --> 00:42:22.040
Dad...

587
00:42:22.165 --> 00:42:27.211
Back in the day. people used to buy
Christmas Seals. right?

588
00:42:27.336 --> 00:42:28.755
Feels like a bygone era.

589
00:42:28.880 --> 00:42:30.423
But I saw it on the internet.

590
00:42:30.548 --> 00:42:34.302
Korea has the number one rate of TB
of all the OECD countries.

591
00:42:34.427 --> 00:42:37.930
But she's still working.
as if nothing's wrong.

592
00:42:38.056 --> 00:42:39.974
With a kid like Da-song
in the house.

593
00:42:40.099 --> 00:42:43.311
So you've got a young kid
like Da-song in the house.

594
00:42:43.436 --> 00:42:46.522
and a TB patient is doing dishes.
cooking. spraying spittle...

595
00:42:46.647 --> 00:42:48.107
Stop it. please!

596
00:42:48.232 --> 00:42:49.650
(Phone buzzes)

597
00:42:52.737 --> 00:42:54.363
DAD: ARRIVING IN 3 MINS

598
00:43:22.266 --> 00:43:24.310
(Coughing and spluttering)

599
00:43:41.327 --> 00:43:44.997
If you get the chance.
this'll be the icing on the cake.

600
00:43:46.666 --> 00:43:48.501
(Violent coughing)

601
00:44:15.528 --> 00:44:17.196
MADAME

602
00:44:17.321 --> 00:44:19.115
2ND FLOOR SAUNA ROOM

603
00:44:19.240 --> 00:44:21.325
DON'T LET HER SEE YOU

604
00:44:30.710 --> 00:44:32.461
- Have a seat.
- Yes.

605
00:44:34.505 --> 00:44:39.427
Mr. Kim. please don't tell any of this
to my husband. okay?

606
00:44:39.552 --> 00:44:40.720
Understood.

607
00:44:40.845 --> 00:44:45.558
If he hears I brought a TB patient
into our home.

608
00:44:45.683 --> 00:44:48.311
I'll be hanged and quartered!

609
00:44:48.436 --> 00:44:50.438
Don't worry. Madame.

610
00:44:50.563 --> 00:44:54.150
And if I may presume
to say one thing.

611
00:44:54.275 --> 00:44:57.778
I have no feelings against that woman.

612
00:44:57.904 --> 00:45:05.203
I felt I had to speak up for the sake
of public health and hygiene.

613
00:45:05.328 --> 00:45:09.081
But this could be seen
as snitching or...

614
00:45:09.207 --> 00:45:13.252
Don't you worry.
I won't mention the TB.

615
00:45:13.377 --> 00:45:15.755
I'll just make up some excuse
to dismiss her.

616
00:45:15.880 --> 00:45:18.090
Simply and quietly.

617
00:45:19.008 --> 00:45:21.677
It's a proven method.
That's the best.

618
00:45:21.802 --> 00:45:23.679
Okay. then.

619
00:45:34.649 --> 00:45:37.652
Have you... washed your hands?

620
00:45:54.043 --> 00:45:55.461
(Inaudible)

621
00:46:23.281 --> 00:46:27.451
Mr. Kim. do you know
a good braised ribs place?

622
00:46:27.576 --> 00:46:30.663
- Somewhere close by.
- Sure.

623
00:46:30.788 --> 00:46:34.333
- Then you'll be eating out?
- That's right.

624
00:46:35.251 --> 00:46:38.170
Why such a craving
for braised ribs today?

625
00:46:38.296 --> 00:46:41.299
Our old housekeeper
made delicious ribs.

626
00:46:41.424 --> 00:46:44.635
Ah. the one who quit this week?

627
00:46:44.760 --> 00:46:49.473
My wife wouldn't even tell me
why she quit.

628
00:46:52.393 --> 00:46:57.481
Sure. it's easy enough
to hire a new one.

629
00:46:58.649 --> 00:47:03.279
Still. it's a shame.
She was a great housekeeper.

630
00:47:03.404 --> 00:47:04.530
I see.

631
00:47:04.655 --> 00:47:07.033
She kept the house in great shape.

632
00:47:07.158 --> 00:47:09.577
and she knew never to cross the line.

633
00:47:10.411 --> 00:47:13.539
I can't stand people
who cross the line.

634
00:47:13.664 --> 00:47:16.167
Perhaps her one weak point?

635
00:47:17.084 --> 00:47:21.339
Eating too much.
She always ate enough for two.

636
00:47:22.298 --> 00:47:26.093
But considering
all the work she did...

637
00:47:26.218 --> 00:47:31.599
Then you better find someone new.
A new housekeeper.

638
00:47:31.724 --> 00:47:33.684
We're in trouble now.

639
00:47:33.809 --> 00:47:37.980
In a week.
our house will be a rubbish tip!

640
00:47:39.065 --> 00:47:42.026
My clothes will start to smell.

641
00:47:43.319 --> 00:47:46.280
My wife has no talent for housework.

642
00:47:46.405 --> 00:47:49.408
She's bad at cleaning.
and her cooking's awful.

643
00:47:50.451 --> 00:47:52.328
Still. you love her. right?

644
00:48:00.252 --> 00:48:03.339
Of course. I love her.

645
00:48:04.423 --> 00:48:06.384
We'll call it love.

646
00:48:08.135 --> 00:48:10.012
Then. would this help?

647
00:48:14.058 --> 00:48:16.560
"The Care"? What is this?

648
00:48:16.685 --> 00:48:19.105
I just recently found out about them.

649
00:48:19.230 --> 00:48:23.818
How to describe it?
It's like a membership service.

650
00:48:24.777 --> 00:48:31.158
The company provides veteran-grade help
to VIP customers such as yourself.

651
00:48:31.283 --> 00:48:37.164
For example. maids. caregivers.
or drivers like myself.

652
00:48:37.289 --> 00:48:40.209
You can tell from the card.
they're high-class.

653
00:48:40.709 --> 00:48:42.378
Cool design.

654
00:48:43.754 --> 00:48:45.714
How do you know about this company?

655
00:48:45.840 --> 00:48:50.344
They contacted me.
as a veteran-grade driver.

656
00:48:50.469 --> 00:48:52.388
You might say they scouted me.

657
00:48:53.931 --> 00:48:59.895
But when their call came.
I'd already arranged to meet with you.

658
00:49:00.020 --> 00:49:02.648
Ah... I see...

659
00:49:04.191 --> 00:49:07.194
You turned down this famous company
to work for me.

660
00:49:07.945 --> 00:49:09.780
I won't forget that.

661
00:49:10.739 --> 00:49:12.908
Son of a bitch!

662
00:49:14.952 --> 00:49:19.081
Anyway. I can give this card
to my wife. right?

663
00:49:19.206 --> 00:49:22.960
Yes. that's why I brought it up.
No need to mention me.

664
00:49:24.211 --> 00:49:27.590
You can tell her
you found the company yourself.

665
00:49:28.257 --> 00:49:29.758
Sure.

666
00:49:29.884 --> 00:49:32.219
Thanks to you.
I can play the good husband.

667
00:49:32.344 --> 00:49:37.057
On the back. there's a number
for consultations.

668
00:49:37.183 --> 00:49:40.186
- Tell her to call there...
- Eyes on the road.

669
00:49:41.479 --> 00:49:42.897
(Phone rings)

670
00:49:44.773 --> 00:49:48.277
Hello. this is Senior Advisor Yeo
of The Care.

671
00:49:48.402 --> 00:49:52.490
- Yes. this is The Care's main office?
- That's correct.

672
00:49:52.615 --> 00:49:56.035
If she wanted.
she'd be a fucking great con artist.

673
00:49:56.160 --> 00:49:58.871
Isn't her voice tone great?
Takes after me.

674
00:50:00.122 --> 00:50:02.833
From what I've heard.
it's a full membership service?

675
00:50:02.958 --> 00:50:06.795
So you're not currently a member.
I assume?

676
00:50:06.921 --> 00:50:09.465
'That's right.
What steps do I need to take?'

677
00:50:09.590 --> 00:50:13.677
We'll just need to receive
a few documents from you.

678
00:50:13.802 --> 00:50:16.722
Are you ready to write this down?

679
00:50:16.847 --> 00:50:21.227
'Your family register.
citizenship ID cards...

680
00:50:22.478 --> 00:50:25.397
'...documents to prove your income level.

681
00:50:25.523 --> 00:50:27.900
'for example.
the title to your property. etc.'

682
00:50:28.025 --> 00:50:30.152
Our property title? Yes.

683
00:50:38.661 --> 00:50:42.248
- (Da-hye) Wow. peaches!
- You have some too. Mr. Kevin.

684
00:50:42.706 --> 00:50:44.124
Thank you.

685
00:50:52.550 --> 00:50:55.553
Leave it outside the door next time.

686
00:50:55.678 --> 00:50:57.680
- And knock.
- Yes.

687
00:51:00.349 --> 00:51:03.143
- No entering during my lesson!
- Yes. Miss.

688
00:51:05.604 --> 00:51:08.232
- (Dong-ik) Park Da-song!
- Daddy!

689
00:51:08.357 --> 00:51:10.359
(Dong-ik) Where are you?

690
00:51:14.280 --> 00:51:16.407
- Daddy!
- Son!

691
00:51:16.532 --> 00:51:18.200
Walkie-talkies!

692
00:51:18.325 --> 00:51:20.452
- Walkie-talkies?
- (Da-song) Walkie-talkies!

693
00:51:20.578 --> 00:51:23.330
Who do you like better.
your dad or the walkie-talkie?

694
00:51:24.373 --> 00:51:26.917
Da-song. how could you run out
from your lesson?

695
00:51:27.751 --> 00:51:31.922
- When did you buy all this?
- It's no big deal.

696
00:51:32.047 --> 00:51:33.465
Oh?

697
00:51:33.591 --> 00:51:35.426
(Da-song sniffs)

698
00:51:36.093 --> 00:51:39.388
- Oh? (Sniffs)
- (Dong-ik) What is it?

699
00:51:42.016 --> 00:51:44.518
- What's he doing now?
- (Sniffs)

700
00:51:44.643 --> 00:51:46.645
- Da-song. don't do that!
- Oh!

701
00:51:46.770 --> 00:51:49.607
It's the same.
They smell the same.

702
00:51:49.732 --> 00:51:53.277
What are you talking about?
Go up to Jessica.

703
00:51:53.402 --> 00:51:57.156
Jessica smells like that. too.

704
00:51:58.240 --> 00:52:01.827
So do we all need to use
different soap. now?

705
00:52:01.952 --> 00:52:06.957
Dad. we'll need to use different
laundry soap. too. And fabric softener.

706
00:52:07.082 --> 00:52:11.378
You mean doing four separate
loads of laundry each time?

707
00:52:11.503 --> 00:52:15.799
That's not it.
It's the semi-basement smell.

708
00:52:17.134 --> 00:52:19.845
We need to leave this home
to lose the smell.

709
00:52:21.805 --> 00:52:27.394
Anyway. aren't we fortunate
to be worrying about things like this?

710
00:52:27.519 --> 00:52:28.896
(Ki-woo) Sure.

711
00:52:29.021 --> 00:52:32.066
In an age like ours.

712
00:52:32.191 --> 00:52:36.904
when an opening for a security guard
attracts 500 university graduates.

713
00:52:37.029 --> 00:52:39.990
our entire family got hired!

714
00:52:40.115 --> 00:52:42.117
That's right. Dad!

715
00:52:42.785 --> 00:52:45.371
And if we put our four salaries together.

716
00:52:45.496 --> 00:52:49.541
the amount of cash coming
from that house into ours is immense.

717
00:52:50.876 --> 00:52:54.755
Let's offer a prayer of gratitude
to the great Mr. Park.

718
00:52:54.880 --> 00:52:56.131
And to Min!

719
00:52:56.256 --> 00:52:58.926
Ki-woo. that friend of yours
turned into such a fine guy.

720
00:52:59.051 --> 00:53:03.055
and thanks to him we're all...
Fuck. not again!

721
00:53:03.180 --> 00:53:05.265
(Drunk sings tunelessly)

722
00:53:08.102 --> 00:53:11.522
- That arsehole's dead.
- (Ki-jung) Ki-woo's on the rampage!

723
00:53:11.647 --> 00:53:14.024
(Ki-taek) Don't overdo it!

724
00:53:15.109 --> 00:53:17.569
Use this instead.

725
00:53:21.281 --> 00:53:22.783
Damn you!

726
00:53:25.411 --> 00:53:28.539
Get a fucking grip! Get a grip!

727
00:53:30.874 --> 00:53:32.334
Wow!

728
00:53:32.459 --> 00:53:33.877
(Ki-jung giggles)

729
00:53:36.505 --> 00:53:38.841
It's a deluge!

730
00:53:54.982 --> 00:53:59.319
Current weather is clear. over.
The clouds are moving.

731
00:53:59.445 --> 00:54:03.282
- 'But they're not rain clouds. over.'
- I hear you. over.

732
00:54:03.407 --> 00:54:09.747
Currently your sister's lip
is pouting like a duck's bill.

733
00:54:09.872 --> 00:54:12.666
She's super annoyed. over.

734
00:54:12.791 --> 00:54:17.671
Can't I stay home and study English?
And call Kevin?

735
00:54:17.796 --> 00:54:21.091
Hey! Don't make a scene
just as we're leaving.

736
00:54:21.216 --> 00:54:23.510
If we have to go. let's have fun.

737
00:54:23.635 --> 00:54:27.097
- Da-hye. this is no ordinary camping trip.
- That's right.

738
00:54:27.222 --> 00:54:29.224
How could you miss
your brother's birthday?

739
00:54:29.349 --> 00:54:32.394
- No way!
- Even your busy father's taking time off.

740
00:54:32.519 --> 00:54:35.189
Right! If you don't go. you'll regret it.

741
00:54:37.816 --> 00:54:39.943
Oh. right.
You know the beam projector?

742
00:54:40.068 --> 00:54:42.863
- The outdoor theatre?
- Right. bring the outdoor beam projector.

743
00:54:42.988 --> 00:54:48.076
- Yes.
- And look for Da-song's camping raincoat.

744
00:54:48.202 --> 00:54:49.870
He loves it when it rains.

745
00:54:50.454 --> 00:54:54.500
You remember now?
Zoonie. Berry. and Foofoo.

746
00:54:54.625 --> 00:54:58.545
- Zoonie and Berry get this.
- Yes. Natural Balance Original Ultra.

747
00:54:58.670 --> 00:55:00.881
Right. and for Foofoo...

748
00:55:01.340 --> 00:55:03.884
- Japanese crab sticks.
- Yes.

749
00:55:04.009 --> 00:55:07.054
When you walk Zoonie.
give him a long leash.

750
00:55:07.179 --> 00:55:09.890
He needs to run around
to feel happy.

751
00:55:10.015 --> 00:55:12.684
He's like the canine version
of Da-song!

752
00:55:38.585 --> 00:55:43.465
Son! Why are you lying down outside?

753
00:55:43.590 --> 00:55:46.051
Isn't he hot out there?

754
00:55:46.885 --> 00:55:51.431
I'm gazing at the sky from home.

755
00:55:53.267 --> 00:55:54.977
It's so great.

756
00:55:58.146 --> 00:56:01.650
- Mum. you want some water?
- (Chung-sook) There's sparkling. right?

757
00:56:01.775 --> 00:56:04.486
Ki-jung. want some water?

758
00:56:04.611 --> 00:56:06.446
Telepathy! Thank you.

759
00:56:22.921 --> 00:56:25.215
(All) Oh. oh. oh...

760
00:56:28.802 --> 00:56:30.929
- Hoo-yah!
- (Ki-jung) Wow!

761
00:56:31.054 --> 00:56:32.848
(All exclaim)

762
00:56:32.973 --> 00:56:35.350
(Ki-taek) Wow.
all these varieties of alcohol.

763
00:56:36.810 --> 00:56:40.147
Dad!
Let me add another to the mix.

764
00:56:40.272 --> 00:56:41.690
Ah...

765
00:56:42.566 --> 00:56:44.359
This is pretty classy.

766
00:56:45.193 --> 00:56:49.239
Rain falling on the lawn.
as we sip our whiskey.

767
00:56:50.532 --> 00:56:54.912
Ki-woo. what's that yellow notebook
you've been carrying?

768
00:56:55.829 --> 00:56:57.164
This?

769
00:56:58.248 --> 00:57:00.959
- It's Da-hye's diary.
- (Chung-sook) Her diary?

770
00:57:01.084 --> 00:57:05.005
What a scumbag.
How could you read her diary?

771
00:57:05.797 --> 00:57:11.136
Just so we can understand
each other deeper.

772
00:57:11.261 --> 00:57:13.931
Fuck. are you two dating?

773
00:57:14.056 --> 00:57:18.143
I'm serious. She really likes me too.

774
00:57:20.395 --> 00:57:21.813
A while back...

775
00:57:22.773 --> 00:57:24.816
Oh. never mind.

776
00:57:24.942 --> 00:57:28.195
When she enters university.
I'll officially ask her out.

777
00:57:28.320 --> 00:57:29.738
Seriously.

778
00:57:34.242 --> 00:57:36.244
My son!

779
00:57:36.370 --> 00:57:40.749
Then this house
will be your in-laws' house?

780
00:57:43.377 --> 00:57:44.711
That's right.

781
00:57:44.836 --> 00:57:48.340
Fuck. then I'm washing dishes
at my daughter-in-law's?

782
00:57:48.465 --> 00:57:51.843
Sure. washing
your daughter-in-law's socks!

783
00:57:51.969 --> 00:57:53.387
(Cackling)

784
00:58:03.647 --> 00:58:09.152
I like her. She's a good kid.

785
00:58:09.277 --> 00:58:13.281
She's pretty. but she's not wild.

786
00:58:14.282 --> 00:58:18.286
Well. now that we're daydreaming...

787
00:58:19.830 --> 00:58:22.416
If Da-hye and I get married.

788
00:58:22.541 --> 00:58:26.628
we can bring in actors
to be my mum and dad.

789
00:58:27.170 --> 00:58:32.300
Look at her. She got so many jobs
acting in weddings last year.

790
00:58:32.426 --> 00:58:36.722
(Sighs) I even caught the bouquet
from a bitch I'd never met.

791
00:58:36.847 --> 00:58:39.725
If you get the bouquet.
they pay an extra $10.

792
00:58:39.850 --> 00:58:41.977
(Chung-sook) That's how
your acting got so good.

793
00:58:42.102 --> 00:58:47.524
Acting is one thing.
but this family is so gullible. right?

794
00:58:47.649 --> 00:58:51.653
- (Chung-sook) The madame. especially.
- You said it.

795
00:58:53.447 --> 00:58:56.867
She's so naive. and nice.

796
00:58:56.992 --> 00:58:59.077
She's rich but still nice.

797
00:58:59.202 --> 00:59:01.496
Not "rich but still nice".

798
00:59:01.621 --> 00:59:05.292
"Nice because she's rich." You know?

799
00:59:05.792 --> 00:59:12.090
Hell. if I had all this money...

800
00:59:13.467 --> 00:59:17.429
...I'd be nice too!

801
00:59:17.554 --> 00:59:19.139
Even nicer!

802
00:59:19.264 --> 00:59:21.475
That's true. Your mum's right.

803
00:59:21.600 --> 00:59:24.019
Rich people are naive.
No resentments.

804
00:59:24.144 --> 00:59:26.354
No creases on them.

805
00:59:26.480 --> 00:59:29.900
It all gets ironed out.
Money is an iron.

806
00:59:30.025 --> 00:59:32.360
Those creases all get smoothed out.

807
00:59:32.486 --> 00:59:33.904
Hey. Ki-woo.

808
00:59:34.654 --> 00:59:39.409
You know that driver. Yoon?
Was it Yoon?

809
00:59:39.951 --> 00:59:43.914
- The driver before me.
- (Ki-woo) Yeah. Yoon.

810
00:59:44.039 --> 00:59:48.418
He must be working
somewhere else now. right?

811
00:59:48.543 --> 00:59:50.879
Sure. he must be.

812
00:59:51.004 --> 00:59:54.299
He's young. got a nice physique.

813
00:59:54.758 --> 00:59:57.677
He must've found a better job.

814
00:59:57.803 --> 00:59:59.763
Fucking hell!

815
01:00:00.931 --> 01:00:03.350
What's with her now?

816
01:00:03.475 --> 01:00:09.397
We're the ones who need help.
Worry about us. okay?

817
01:00:10.107 --> 01:00:13.443
Dad! Come on. Dad!

818
01:00:13.568 --> 01:00:17.906
Just focus on us. okay? On us!

819
01:00:18.031 --> 01:00:19.658
Not Driver Yoon!

820
01:00:19.783 --> 01:00:22.285
- But me. please!
- (Thunderclap)

821
01:00:22.410 --> 01:00:24.621
Awesome timing. huh?

822
01:00:24.746 --> 01:00:28.542
She speaks.
and the lightning crashes!

823
01:00:30.502 --> 01:00:32.879
Hey. Jessica. Cheers.

824
01:00:34.339 --> 01:00:40.095
Hey. when I went up before.
and you were in the bath...

825
01:00:40.220 --> 01:00:41.805
What about it?

826
01:00:42.556 --> 01:00:46.059
How to put it? You fit in here.

827
01:00:46.184 --> 01:00:48.937
This rich house suits you.
Not like us.

828
01:00:49.062 --> 01:00:50.856
- Fuck off.
- I'm serious.

829
01:00:50.981 --> 01:00:55.944
Dad. before. she was lying back
in the tub. watching TV.

830
01:00:56.069 --> 01:00:58.405
like she's lived here for years.

831
01:01:00.282 --> 01:01:06.204
Speaking of which.
if this became our house.

832
01:01:06.329 --> 01:01:10.500
if we lived here.
which room would you want?

833
01:01:10.625 --> 01:01:15.797
What room in this masterwork
by the great Namgoong?

834
01:01:15.922 --> 01:01:17.757
Fuck. I don't know.

835
01:01:17.883 --> 01:01:21.136
Get me the house first.
then I'll think about that.

836
01:01:22.053 --> 01:01:24.556
We live here now. don't we?

837
01:01:24.681 --> 01:01:28.435
Getting drunk in the living room.

838
01:01:28.560 --> 01:01:31.521
Right. we live here. Why not?

839
01:01:31.646 --> 01:01:36.318
This is our home right now. It's cosy.

840
01:01:36.443 --> 01:01:39.613
Cosy? Are you feeling cosy?

841
01:01:39.738 --> 01:01:44.326
Sure. but suppose Park walked
through that door right now.

842
01:01:45.035 --> 01:01:49.873
What about your dad?
He'd run and hide like a cockroach.

843
01:01:50.457 --> 01:01:52.834
Kids. you know at our house.

844
01:01:52.959 --> 01:01:58.673
when you turn on the light.
and the cockroaches scatter?

845
01:01:58.798 --> 01:02:00.926
You know what I mean?

846
01:02:01.051 --> 01:02:04.221
I'm getting fucking tired of this.

847
01:02:05.096 --> 01:02:06.765
- A cockroach?
- Yeah.

848
01:02:10.769 --> 01:02:13.730
- Huh? What's wrong?
- What's the matter?

849
01:02:13.855 --> 01:02:17.234
Dad. don't do that. You only live once.

850
01:02:20.820 --> 01:02:22.322
(Laughing)

851
01:02:24.658 --> 01:02:26.451
(Ki-Jung) What the hell?

852
01:02:26.576 --> 01:02:29.579
- I fooled you. didn't I?
- (Ki-woo) Jesus. Dad.

853
01:02:29.704 --> 01:02:33.750
I fooled you too. Ki-woo?
Did it look for real?

854
01:02:33.875 --> 01:02:37.879
If it was for real. I'd fucking kill you.

855
01:02:38.004 --> 01:02:41.424
What is this? Fucking puppy.

856
01:02:42.300 --> 01:02:43.843
(Doorbell rings)

857
01:02:47.264 --> 01:02:49.474
Who is it at this hour?

858
01:02:49.599 --> 01:02:51.434
What is it?

859
01:02:57.649 --> 01:03:01.653
- (Ki-woo) What's she doing here?
- The old housekeeper?

860
01:03:02.237 --> 01:03:04.489
- What's she here for?
- (Continues ringing)

861
01:03:04.614 --> 01:03:08.493
She won't stop ringing it.

862
01:03:09.577 --> 01:03:12.414
(Chung-sook) Raising a racket.

863
01:03:13.915 --> 01:03:19.379
- Who is it?
- 'Oh. hello. I'm...

864
01:03:19.504 --> 01:03:22.299
- 'The madame's not in. right?'
- Eh?

865
01:03:22.424 --> 01:03:26.678
'I worked here for a very long time.

866
01:03:27.429 --> 01:03:33.059
'Above the monitor there.
you see a photo of three dogs. right?

867
01:03:33.184 --> 01:03:39.149
- 'Zoonie. Berry. Foofoo...'
- I get it. but why are you here?

868
01:03:39.274 --> 01:03:44.029
'You're my successor
as housekeeper. right?'

869
01:03:44.154 --> 01:03:45.572
('Laughter')

870
01:03:48.950 --> 01:03:50.493
'Anyway...

871
01:03:51.244 --> 01:03:54.539
'I'm very sorry to call on you so late.

872
01:03:54.664 --> 01:03:56.291
'It's just that...

873
01:03:56.750 --> 01:04:03.590
'I forgot something in the basement
under the kitchen.'

874
01:04:04.341 --> 01:04:10.305
When I left.
they pushed me out so quickly...

875
01:04:13.850 --> 01:04:16.186
'Would you let me in?'

876
01:04:18.021 --> 01:04:19.856
What do we do?

877
01:04:20.482 --> 01:04:22.650
This isn't in the plan.

878
01:04:30.492 --> 01:04:31.993
Sorry for the trouble.

879
01:04:32.911 --> 01:04:35.038
- This way.
- Yes. thank you.

880
01:04:37.415 --> 01:04:39.709
You can put your raincoat...

881
01:04:39.834 --> 01:04:41.878
I'll just be a second.

882
01:04:42.754 --> 01:04:46.424
Quite a meal there.
That'll be a job to clean up.

883
01:04:46.549 --> 01:04:49.636
But what did you leave below?

884
01:04:54.349 --> 01:04:56.726
Want to come down with me?

885
01:04:57.811 --> 01:05:01.106
(Chung-sook) Eh?
Well. just go ahead.

886
01:05:01.231 --> 01:05:02.649
(Giggling)

887
01:05:26.798 --> 01:05:28.425
(Sighs heavily)

888
01:05:41.020 --> 01:05:42.689
(Groaning)

889
01:05:46.401 --> 01:05:48.486
(Intense groaning)

890
01:05:54.868 --> 01:05:57.829
Help me push this!

891
01:05:58.288 --> 01:06:00.457
Pull it! From over there!

892
01:06:02.333 --> 01:06:03.793
Pull!

893
01:06:05.795 --> 01:06:07.422
Pull it hard!

894
01:06:11.217 --> 01:06:13.136
Are you okay?

895
01:06:13.928 --> 01:06:16.097
Did I scare you?

896
01:06:18.057 --> 01:06:19.392
Thank you!

897
01:06:20.768 --> 01:06:22.187
Thank you.

898
01:06:30.236 --> 01:06:32.071
- Honey!
- What the...?

899
01:06:33.781 --> 01:06:36.367
(Housekeeper) Hey! Honey!

900
01:06:37.494 --> 01:06:38.912
Honey!

901
01:06:41.539 --> 01:06:44.876
- (Chung-sook) Wait!
- (Housekeeper) Honey. I'm here!

902
01:06:45.001 --> 01:06:46.836
(Chung-sook) What's all this?

903
01:06:48.463 --> 01:06:50.256
(Panting)

904
01:06:50.381 --> 01:06:53.510
- (Man) Honey. I'm fine.
- (Housekeeper) No. you're not!

905
01:06:53.968 --> 01:06:56.304
- (Man) I'm fine. really.
- (Housekeeper) How can you say that?

906
01:06:56.429 --> 01:06:59.015
- But I'm really hungry.
- Suck this.

907
01:06:59.140 --> 01:07:04.437
How many days has it been?
You must've been so hungry.

908
01:07:06.272 --> 01:07:10.318
It's okay.
She's a nice woman. She let me in.

909
01:07:10.443 --> 01:07:14.239
There was an iron plate for grilling meat.
It was wedged under the shelf.

910
01:07:14.364 --> 01:07:18.368
(Man) So that's why.
I couldn't open it from the inside.

911
01:07:18.826 --> 01:07:22.372
- What's going on here?
- I know you must be startled.

912
01:07:22.497 --> 01:07:25.041
I would be too. in this situation.

913
01:07:25.166 --> 01:07:29.712
But as two fellow workers...
Right. Chung-sook?

914
01:07:29.837 --> 01:07:32.382
How do you know my name?

915
01:07:32.507 --> 01:07:37.262
To be honest. I'm still texting
with the boy Da-song.

916
01:07:37.971 --> 01:07:42.559
I knew they were going camping.
so I came today.

917
01:07:42.684 --> 01:07:46.396
I wanted to speak to you alone.
Talking about...

918
01:07:49.190 --> 01:07:51.568
Don't worry. Chung-sook.

919
01:07:51.693 --> 01:07:55.405
I cut the wire on the CCTV
by the gate.

920
01:07:55.530 --> 01:07:59.075
Nobody knows I came.
Isn't that good. sis?

921
01:07:59.200 --> 01:08:01.286
Don't call me sis.

922
01:08:01.411 --> 01:08:04.038
Sis. my name is Moon-gwang.

923
01:08:04.581 --> 01:08:08.918
This is my hubbie Oh Geun-sae.
Say hello. honey.

924
01:08:09.043 --> 01:08:12.380
This tastes great.
What happened to your face?

925
01:08:12.505 --> 01:08:15.758
I'll tell you later.

926
01:08:15.883 --> 01:08:19.762
So you'd steal food every day
while working in the kitchen.

927
01:08:19.887 --> 01:08:22.098
- Feeding your husband.
- Not at all!

928
01:08:22.223 --> 01:08:25.685
I bought all his food with my salary.

929
01:08:25.810 --> 01:08:28.813
That's so unfair!

930
01:08:28.938 --> 01:08:31.691
But how long has your husband
been down here?

931
01:08:31.816 --> 01:08:34.193
Hold on a sec...
Four years?

932
01:08:34.902 --> 01:08:37.697
Four years. three months
and 17 days.

933
01:08:37.822 --> 01:08:39.490
Right. it's June now.

934
01:08:40.074 --> 01:08:46.205
Four years ago
when Mr. Namgoong moved to Paris.

935
01:08:46.331 --> 01:08:49.125
in the time before
Mr. Park's family moved in.

936
01:08:49.250 --> 01:08:52.920
I brought my husband down here.

937
01:08:53.046 --> 01:08:58.217
Many rich houses have secret bunkers.
where you can hide

938
01:08:58.343 --> 01:09:02.722
in case North Korea attacks.
or if creditors break in.

939
01:09:02.847 --> 01:09:09.020
But it seems Mr. Namgoong
was a bit embarrassed about this.

940
01:09:09.145 --> 01:09:12.982
because he never mentioned it
to Mr. Park's family.

941
01:09:13.107 --> 01:09:16.986
- So only I know about it...
- So that's how it happened.

942
01:09:17.111 --> 01:09:21.199
But now that I know.
I've no choice but to call the police!

943
01:09:21.324 --> 01:09:23.493
No. please. sis!

944
01:09:24.369 --> 01:09:26.663
As fellow members of the needy.
please don't.

945
01:09:26.788 --> 01:09:32.001
- I'm not needy!
- But we're needy!

946
01:09:32.126 --> 01:09:36.506
We've no house. no money.
only debts!

947
01:09:36.631 --> 01:09:38.091
Sis. please!

948
01:09:38.216 --> 01:09:42.428
Even after four years of hiding.
those debt collectors won't give up.

949
01:09:42.553 --> 01:09:46.683
They're still searching for him.
threatening to stab him.

950
01:09:46.808 --> 01:09:49.143
You used loan sharks?

951
01:09:49.268 --> 01:09:51.479
(Geun-sae) It's all my fault.

952
01:09:51.604 --> 01:09:53.523
The Taiwan cake shop.

953
01:09:53.648 --> 01:09:57.777
My Taiwanese Wangshui
castella shop went bust.

954
01:09:57.902 --> 01:09:59.946
I was overwhelmed by debt.

955
01:10:00.071 --> 01:10:03.574
- (Moon-gwang) Please take this.
- (Chung-sook) What's that?

956
01:10:03.700 --> 01:10:07.870
It's not much. just a modest sum.

957
01:10:07.995 --> 01:10:11.124
But we'll send it to you every month.

958
01:10:11.249 --> 01:10:15.837
In return. just once every two days.
please leave him some food.

959
01:10:16.879 --> 01:10:19.465
No. no. just once a week.

960
01:10:20.133 --> 01:10:22.593
There's a refrigerator here.
Just once a week.

961
01:10:22.719 --> 01:10:25.096
You've got some nerve!
I'm calling the police.

962
01:10:25.221 --> 01:10:26.723
Sis!

963
01:10:26.848 --> 01:10:28.891
(Screaming)

964
01:10:29.016 --> 01:10:31.978
- (Geun-sae) Who is that?
- (Moans of pain)

965
01:10:33.438 --> 01:10:35.231
Wait... Jessica?

966
01:10:36.065 --> 01:10:37.859
Mr. Kim? What the hell?

967
01:10:39.610 --> 01:10:42.113
- (Ki-woo) Dad. my ankle!
- You okay? Sorry.

968
01:10:42.238 --> 01:10:44.115
Dad. my foot!

969
01:10:44.240 --> 01:10:48.286
- Don't call me Dad.
- Oh? Oh?

970
01:10:50.413 --> 01:10:52.498
(Moon-gwang laughs)

971
01:10:53.166 --> 01:10:56.711
I thought it was weird
when the driver was sacked.

972
01:10:58.045 --> 01:11:01.007
- Let's talk things over.
- (Moon-gwang) What the hell?

973
01:11:01.132 --> 01:11:03.384
- Are you some family of charlatans?
- So. sis...

974
01:11:03.509 --> 01:11:06.179
Don't fucking call me sis.
you filthy bitch!

975
01:11:06.304 --> 01:11:11.768
I'm gonna send this video
to the madame. how about that?

976
01:11:11.893 --> 01:11:13.478
'Dad. my foot!'

977
01:11:13.603 --> 01:11:15.688
No reception in the basement. right?

978
01:11:16.397 --> 01:11:18.316
- The phone works fine.
- Fuck.

979
01:11:18.441 --> 01:11:23.029
Ma'am. to be honest.
the jobs we have here...

980
01:11:23.154 --> 01:11:26.157
Shut up! It's too late now!

981
01:11:26.282 --> 01:11:29.744
Let's all go to jail!
We're fucking going down!

982
01:11:29.869 --> 01:11:32.747
Lady. are you crazy?

983
01:11:33.498 --> 01:11:38.669
If they see that video.
Mr. Park and his wife will be so shocked!

984
01:11:38.795 --> 01:11:41.881
What did those nice people
ever do wrong?

985
01:11:42.715 --> 01:11:45.259
- Why do this to them?
- Stop right there!

986
01:11:45.384 --> 01:11:47.762
Or I'll push the 'send' button.

987
01:11:47.887 --> 01:11:49.388
Follow me.

988
01:11:50.097 --> 01:11:52.475
(Ki-woo) Calm down. ma'am.

989
01:11:56.062 --> 01:11:58.105
(Ki-taek) Don't push.

990
01:11:59.357 --> 01:12:04.070
Let's go up. honey.
Time for you to get some fresh air!

991
01:12:09.951 --> 01:12:12.245
(♪ Easy-listening tune)

992
01:12:15.248 --> 01:12:17.083
(Geun-sae giggles)

993
01:12:21.337 --> 01:12:27.760
Honey. this 'send' button
is like a missile launcher.

994
01:12:27.885 --> 01:12:30.346
What do you mean. honey?

995
01:12:30.471 --> 01:12:35.434
If we threaten to push it.
those people can't do anything.

996
01:12:35.560 --> 01:12:39.814
It's like a North Korean rocket.
A North Korean missile button!

997
01:12:41.357 --> 01:12:45.027
Today our beloved
Great Leader Kim Jong-un.

998
01:12:45.152 --> 01:12:47.947
after witnessing
the charlatan family video.

999
01:12:48.072 --> 01:12:51.033
was unable to contain
his shock and fury

1000
01:12:51.158 --> 01:12:54.370
at their wicked. despicable provocation!

1001
01:12:54.495 --> 01:12:56.581
I've missed your jokes. honey.

1002
01:12:56.706 --> 01:13:00.918
Therefore our Great Leader.
in this age of denuclearization.

1003
01:13:01.043 --> 01:13:06.799
has commanded that the nation's
last remaining nuclear warhead

1004
01:13:06.924 --> 01:13:09.343
be driven down the throats
of this wicked family!

1005
01:13:09.468 --> 01:13:14.557
No one can imitate North Korean
news anchors like you!

1006
01:13:14.682 --> 01:13:19.270
With their stinking guts serving
as the last nuclear graveyard.

1007
01:13:19.395 --> 01:13:24.275
our Dear Leader's wish to denuclearize
and bring world peace can...

1008
01:13:24.400 --> 01:13:26.319
Hands in the air. you fuckers!

1009
01:13:26.444 --> 01:13:27.862
Higher!

1010
01:13:30.031 --> 01:13:32.033
You scumbag family.

1011
01:13:32.158 --> 01:13:34.076
- Husband?
- Husband.

1012
01:13:34.201 --> 01:13:35.953
- (Moon-gwang) Wife?
- Yes.

1013
01:13:36.078 --> 01:13:37.705
- (Moon-gwang) Son?
- Yes.

1014
01:13:37.830 --> 01:13:39.123
- (Moon-gwang) Daughter?
- Daughter.

1015
01:13:39.248 --> 01:13:41.083
(Moon-gwang) You neanderthals.

1016
01:13:41.208 --> 01:13:45.463
Is that all you can think to do.
drink yourselves stupid?

1017
01:13:45.588 --> 01:13:50.968
In this home suffused
with Mr. Namgoong's creative spirit?

1018
01:13:51.093 --> 01:13:53.554
You cretins!
What do you know about art?

1019
01:13:53.679 --> 01:13:56.432
What would they know?

1020
01:13:56.557 --> 01:14:04.106
When the sun was nice.
we'd bask in those sunbeams. right?

1021
01:14:05.191 --> 01:14:09.612
'At such moments.
we could feel his artistic touch.'

1022
01:14:09.737 --> 01:14:11.822
(♪ Easy-listening ballad)

1023
01:14:31.717 --> 01:14:33.260
(Moon-gwang screams)

1024
01:14:36.180 --> 01:14:38.474
(♪ Music over audio)

1025
01:14:57.660 --> 01:15:01.038
Give it to me!

1026
01:15:20.099 --> 01:15:22.184
Good job!

1027
01:15:22.309 --> 01:15:24.520
- Delete it!
- (Telephone rings)

1028
01:15:24.645 --> 01:15:27.231
Careful. don't send it by accident.

1029
01:15:31.360 --> 01:15:32.778
(Ringing)

1030
01:15:41.912 --> 01:15:43.581
Hello?

1031
01:15:43.706 --> 01:15:46.876
Listen. do you know
how to make ram-don?

1032
01:15:47.710 --> 01:15:49.086
Ram-don?

1033
01:15:49.211 --> 01:15:52.798
Da-song likes ram-don
more than anything.

1034
01:15:52.923 --> 01:15:56.427
If you boil the water now.
the timing will be perfect.

1035
01:15:56.552 --> 01:15:59.388
'There's sirloin in the fridge.
add that too.'

1036
01:15:59.513 --> 01:16:01.057
So. the camping...?

1037
01:16:01.182 --> 01:16:04.769
'Oh. my god. what a disaster.'

1038
01:16:05.478 --> 01:16:10.649
The river overflowed
and everyone was packing their tents.

1039
01:16:10.775 --> 01:16:13.819
but Da-song was crying
and refusing to go home.

1040
01:16:13.944 --> 01:16:18.199
'Anyway. ram-don
as soon as we walk in. okay?'

1041
01:16:18.324 --> 01:16:20.743
Then you're almost here?

1042
01:16:20.868 --> 01:16:23.329
Eight minutes. according to the GPS.

1043
01:16:23.454 --> 01:16:27.958
- You arrive in eight minutes.
- 'Start boiling the water right away!'

1044
01:16:32.546 --> 01:16:34.590
What the hell is ram-don?

1045
01:16:43.349 --> 01:16:44.809
(Ki-taek) Move. quickly!

1046
01:16:46.060 --> 01:16:48.020
Hurry!

1047
01:16:48.145 --> 01:16:49.939
(Geun-sae chuckles)

1048
01:16:54.902 --> 01:16:56.612
RAMEN / UDON

1049
01:16:58.280 --> 01:17:01.158
Dad. I can't drag her any further!

1050
01:17:12.378 --> 01:17:14.088
What are you doing?

1051
01:17:15.714 --> 01:17:17.049
Dad!

1052
01:17:20.094 --> 01:17:23.305
Go quickly and help upstairs!

1053
01:17:31.063 --> 01:17:32.940
Take this!

1054
01:17:34.191 --> 01:17:36.193
(Entrance keypad beeping)

1055
01:17:50.791 --> 01:17:52.710
Ah. welcome home.

1056
01:17:52.835 --> 01:17:55.963
Da-song. look. Let's eat ram-don.

1057
01:17:58.382 --> 01:17:59.717
Da-song!

1058
01:18:02.469 --> 01:18:03.804
Da-song!

1059
01:18:10.728 --> 01:18:12.354
(Moon-gwang) Madame!

1060
01:18:14.690 --> 01:18:16.483
(Footsteps approaching)

1061
01:18:22.865 --> 01:18:24.074
(Gasps)

1062
01:18:30.706 --> 01:18:33.709
- Why don't you just eat the ram-don?
- Shall I?

1063
01:18:33.834 --> 01:18:36.921
No. wait. I can give it to my husband.

1064
01:18:37.046 --> 01:18:39.048
There's sirloin in here.

1065
01:18:41.634 --> 01:18:45.137
It's cooked through?
Medium well done?

1066
01:19:10.204 --> 01:19:16.377
(Geun-sae) ♪ Returning after a day's work.
I love you so much. Mr. Park!

1067
01:19:16.502 --> 01:19:22.675
♪ Home from the office.
Mr. Park is off duty now

1068
01:19:22.800 --> 01:19:24.510
(Retching and coughing)

1069
01:19:24.635 --> 01:19:28.889
♪ Returning after a day's work.
I love you so much. Mr. Park... ♪

1070
01:19:29.014 --> 01:19:31.183
- What are you doing?
- Shut up!

1071
01:19:42.569 --> 01:19:46.240
- Honey. do you want some ram-don?
- Da-song doesn't want it?

1072
01:19:46.365 --> 01:19:48.659
- No.
- No. I'm tired. I'm going to bed.

1073
01:19:49.326 --> 01:19:51.996
Why are you staring?

1074
01:19:53.247 --> 01:19:56.625
Mr. Park. you feed me and house me.

1075
01:19:56.750 --> 01:19:58.752
(Shouts in English) Respect!

1076
01:19:58.877 --> 01:20:04.091
- You... You do this every day?
- Sure.

1077
01:20:04.216 --> 01:20:08.304
I even send whole sentences
to thank him.

1078
01:20:08.429 --> 01:20:11.682
- Someone of your age should know it.
- Know what?

1079
01:20:11.807 --> 01:20:13.600
Morse Code.

1080
01:20:14.226 --> 01:20:17.646
That sensor's going batty.

1081
01:20:26.405 --> 01:20:29.867
Da-song will know it.
since he's a Scout.

1082
01:20:29.992 --> 01:20:35.289
It's ridiculous. right?
Running around. trying to please a kid.

1083
01:20:35.414 --> 01:20:37.374
He's not some kind of prince.

1084
01:20:37.499 --> 01:20:39.918
He's the youngest. It's common.

1085
01:20:41.253 --> 01:20:42.588
Please understand.

1086
01:20:43.339 --> 01:20:46.759
Da-song is a bit... unwell.

1087
01:20:47.343 --> 01:20:50.054
He's receiving trauma therapy
and art therapy.

1088
01:20:51.305 --> 01:20:53.307
There was an incident.

1089
01:20:53.432 --> 01:20:54.975
What incident?

1090
01:20:55.100 --> 01:20:58.187
Sis. you believe in ghosts. too?

1091
01:21:00.105 --> 01:21:03.734
Da-song saw a ghost in the house
when he was in primary school.

1092
01:21:10.324 --> 01:21:12.951
He had a birthday party
at home that day.

1093
01:21:13.077 --> 01:21:15.537
Late that night.
when everyone was sleeping.

1094
01:21:15.662 --> 01:21:20.209
Da-song crept down to the kitchen
and took the cake out.

1095
01:21:20.334 --> 01:21:23.379
The whipped cream
on that cake was amazing.

1096
01:21:23.504 --> 01:21:26.090
Even in bed.
he couldn't stop thinking about it.

1097
01:21:26.799 --> 01:21:32.012
'So Da-song was sitting there.
eating his cake.'

1098
01:21:41.480 --> 01:21:44.525
"Ah!" he screamed.
and I ran downstairs.

1099
01:21:45.317 --> 01:21:47.027
He was all...

1100
01:21:47.861 --> 01:21:52.908
His eyes rolled back in his head.
convulsions. foam in his mouth.

1101
01:21:55.119 --> 01:21:57.371
Have you ever seen a child
have a seizure?

1102
01:21:57.496 --> 01:21:58.580
No.

1103
01:21:58.705 --> 01:22:03.669
They need treatment within 15 minutes.
or they're done for.

1104
01:22:03.794 --> 01:22:07.798
That's the time you have
to reach an emergency room. 15 minutes.

1105
01:22:09.341 --> 01:22:14.721
How can you live in a place like this?

1106
01:22:14.847 --> 01:22:20.018
Well. lots of people live underground.
Especially if you count semi-basements.

1107
01:22:20.144 --> 01:22:24.273
What'|| you do? You don't have a plan?

1108
01:22:25.065 --> 01:22:28.068
I just feel comfortable here.

1109
01:22:29.653 --> 01:22:32.573
It feels like I was born here.

1110
01:22:33.532 --> 01:22:36.577
Maybe I had my wedding here. too.

1111
01:22:37.077 --> 01:22:39.913
As for the National Pension.
I don't qualify.

1112
01:22:41.457 --> 01:22:44.835
In my old age. love will comfort me.

1113
01:22:46.462 --> 01:22:51.383
So. please... let me live down here.

1114
01:22:52.843 --> 01:22:54.595
Oh. anyway...

1115
01:22:55.679 --> 01:23:00.559
my husband was away on business.
so I had to deal with it all.

1116
01:23:01.560 --> 01:23:06.064
Since then. we've always gone out
for his birthday.

1117
01:23:06.190 --> 01:23:08.692
Last year my mother's house.
this year camping.

1118
01:23:08.817 --> 01:23:13.906
Da-song's father says
it's just a part of growing up.

1119
01:23:14.031 --> 01:23:18.452
They say a ghost in the house
brings wealth.

1120
01:23:19.953 --> 01:23:24.666
Actually.
the money's been good recently.

1121
01:23:51.568 --> 01:23:53.278
Thank God!

1122
01:23:56.990 --> 01:23:58.408
(Dog whimpers)

1123
01:24:19.846 --> 01:24:22.808
Just stay there for now.

1124
01:24:33.694 --> 01:24:35.696
(Da-hye) Zoonie. what's wrong?

1125
01:24:38.115 --> 01:24:42.077
Is something under there?
What is it?

1126
01:24:43.704 --> 01:24:45.205
Damn it!

1127
01:24:46.290 --> 01:24:47.541
Mum...

1128
01:24:47.666 --> 01:24:49.876
- How could you?
- What?

1129
01:24:50.002 --> 01:24:53.922
I like ram-don too!
How could you not even ask me?

1130
01:24:54.423 --> 01:24:59.094
Da-song didn't want it.
so you asked dad. then ate it yourself!

1131
01:24:59.219 --> 01:25:02.014
- (Yeon-kyo) Want her to make one?
- (Da-hye) That's not the point!

1132
01:25:02.139 --> 01:25:05.809
- (Dong-ik) Stop fighting over ramen!
- (Da-hye) Why didn't you ask me?

1133
01:25:05.934 --> 01:25:09.146
(Yeon-kyo) Oh. stop it!
Just go to bed. Go and get changed.

1134
01:25:13.025 --> 01:25:14.443
This way.

1135
01:25:16.778 --> 01:25:20.073
- And Ki-jung?
- Under there. Hurry.

1136
01:25:23.577 --> 01:25:25.829
One. two. three! One. two. three!

1137
01:25:25.954 --> 01:25:29.916
- Da-song?
- (Yeon-kyo) Da-song. cut it out!

1138
01:25:30.751 --> 01:25:33.253
He's gone crazy! Get an umbrella.

1139
01:25:33.378 --> 01:25:35.005
Hey. Park Da-song!

1140
01:25:36.381 --> 01:25:40.969
What a monster.
What the hell is he doing?

1141
01:25:41.094 --> 01:25:45.515
(Yeon-kyo) Da-song. it's time for bed!
You know how late it is?

1142
01:25:45.641 --> 01:25:48.226
- Here.
- Honey. here.

1143
01:25:52.105 --> 01:25:58.528
(Dong-ik) Who do you take after
to be so stubborn? Look at this rain!

1144
01:26:04.326 --> 01:26:06.953
OMG. KEVIN.
DA-SONG'S CAMPING IN THE YARD

1145
01:26:10.874 --> 01:26:15.671
(Dong-ik) Hey. channel 3 for emergencies!
Keep it turned on!

1146
01:26:15.796 --> 01:26:18.548
Let me have that.
I can't believe him.

1147
01:26:18.674 --> 01:26:21.927
(Dong-ik) Just leave him.
He'll come in if he's tired.

1148
01:26:22.052 --> 01:26:24.680
- I WANT YOU HERE. HONEY.
- I'M WITH YOU.

1149
01:26:24.805 --> 01:26:28.767
Da-hye. stop using your phone
and go to bed.

1150
01:26:28.892 --> 01:26:31.645
Go to sleep in your room.
We'll take care of things.

1151
01:26:31.770 --> 01:26:36.149
- This is the living room. do you copy?
- (Da-song) 'Copy. over.'

1152
01:26:36.274 --> 01:26:39.945
Daddy is standing by
for emergencies. over.

1153
01:26:40.570 --> 01:26:42.572
'Got it. over.'

1154
01:26:42.698 --> 01:26:44.157
(Dong-ik sighs)

1155
01:26:44.282 --> 01:26:46.076
Is that tent going to leak?

1156
01:26:46.201 --> 01:26:49.621
We ordered it from the USA.
it'll be fine.

1157
01:26:49.746 --> 01:26:52.749
- Should we sleep here?
- Eh?

1158
01:26:52.874 --> 01:26:54.918
We've got a clear view of the tent.

1159
01:26:55.043 --> 01:26:57.754
- Good idea. I'd feel much better.
- Right?

1160
01:26:57.879 --> 01:27:00.048
Let's watch over him as we sleep.

1161
01:27:01.383 --> 01:27:03.301
What a kid!

1162
01:27:12.644 --> 01:27:14.146
Wait a minute.

1163
01:27:14.271 --> 01:27:16.273
(Sniffs) Eh?

1164
01:27:16.398 --> 01:27:20.318
- Where's that smell coming from?
- What smell?

1165
01:27:20.444 --> 01:27:22.154
Mr. Kim's smell.

1166
01:27:22.279 --> 01:27:23.905
- Mr. Kim?
- Hmm...

1167
01:27:24.030 --> 01:27:28.952
- (Yeon-kyo) Not sure what you mean.
- Really? You must've smelled it.

1168
01:27:29.453 --> 01:27:33.290
That smell that wafts through the car.
how'd you describe it?

1169
01:27:33.415 --> 01:27:36.084
- An old man's smell?
- No. no. it's not that.

1170
01:27:36.209 --> 01:27:40.172
What is it?
Like an old radish?

1171
01:27:41.173 --> 01:27:45.927
No. You know when you boil a rag?
It smells like that.

1172
01:27:48.764 --> 01:27:55.187
Anyway... even though he always
seems about to cross the line.

1173
01:27:55.312 --> 01:27:58.482
he never does cross it.
and that's good.

1174
01:27:58.607 --> 01:28:00.442
- I'll give him credit.
- Yeah.

1175
01:28:01.318 --> 01:28:03.862
But that smell crosses the line.

1176
01:28:04.362 --> 01:28:06.531
It powers through
right into the back seat.

1177
01:28:06.990 --> 01:28:09.785
- (Yeon-kyo) How bad can it be?
- I don't know...

1178
01:28:10.786 --> 01:28:13.163
It's hard to describe.

1179
01:28:14.331 --> 01:28:17.959
But you sometimes smell it
on the Underground.

1180
01:28:18.084 --> 01:28:21.171
It's been ages since I've been
on the Underground.

1181
01:28:21.963 --> 01:28:24.966
(Dong-ik) People who ride the subway
have a special smell.

1182
01:28:25.091 --> 01:28:26.593
(Yeon-kyo) Hmm...

1183
01:28:42.651 --> 01:28:45.362
Isn't this like the back seat of the car?

1184
01:28:46.321 --> 01:28:49.491
What if Da-song comes back in?

1185
01:28:50.242 --> 01:28:52.035
Don't worry.

1186
01:28:52.160 --> 01:28:54.913
I can just pull my hand back.

1187
01:29:00.585 --> 01:29:02.087
We shouldn't.

1188
01:29:08.343 --> 01:29:11.471
- Do it clockwise.
- Right.

1189
01:29:15.016 --> 01:29:18.270
You know where.

1190
01:29:30.866 --> 01:29:33.243
(Moaning)

1191
01:29:34.828 --> 01:29:38.331
You still have those cheap panties?

1192
01:29:40.125 --> 01:29:42.627
The ones Yoon's girlfriend left behind.

1193
01:29:44.087 --> 01:29:46.923
If you wear those.
I'll get really fucking hard.

1194
01:29:47.716 --> 01:29:49.551
(Yeon-kyo) Really?

1195
01:29:49.676 --> 01:29:51.720
Then buy me drugs.

1196
01:29:53.305 --> 01:29:55.682
Buy me drugs!

1197
01:29:57.851 --> 01:29:59.811
Eat this instead.

1198
01:30:05.901 --> 01:30:07.319
(Moaning)

1199
01:30:11.323 --> 01:30:12.741
You like it?

1200
01:30:18.663 --> 01:30:20.290
(Dong-ik snores)

1201
01:30:23.126 --> 01:30:24.753
(Snoring)

1202
01:30:33.720 --> 01:30:35.764
THEY'RE PASSED OUT.
SNEAK OUT NOW.

1203
01:31:07.879 --> 01:31:09.881
(Walkie-talkie squelches and beeps)

1204
01:31:10.006 --> 01:31:12.217
(Da-song) 'Emergency!
Emergency. over!

1205
01:31:14.678 --> 01:31:16.137
- 'Emergency!'
- What?

1206
01:31:17.180 --> 01:31:19.808
- What is it? Over.
- Da-song. what's wrong?

1207
01:31:20.392 --> 01:31:22.727
'I can't sleep. over.'

1208
01:31:22.852 --> 01:31:26.564
So stop it and come in. okay?

1209
01:31:26.690 --> 01:31:30.860
- Come and sleep in your soft bed. over.
- Right!

1210
01:31:30.986 --> 01:31:35.198
- 'I don't want to. over.'
- Hey. Park Da-song...

1211
01:31:39.953 --> 01:31:42.580
(Dong-ik) Let's just sleep.

1212
01:31:54.801 --> 01:31:56.219
Hey!

1213
01:33:04.704 --> 01:33:06.706
(Groaning and panting)

1214
01:33:17.509 --> 01:33:21.012
How did it turn out back there?

1215
01:33:22.097 --> 01:33:23.723
(Ki-taek) What?

1216
01:33:25.475 --> 01:33:27.477
The people in the basement.

1217
01:33:30.438 --> 01:33:34.567
Well... I tied them up.

1218
01:33:35.401 --> 01:33:37.237
What will we do now?

1219
01:33:38.488 --> 01:33:39.697
Huh?

1220
01:33:41.825 --> 01:33:44.661
What do we do now?
What's our plan?

1221
01:33:46.079 --> 01:33:52.794
I've been wondering
what Min would do in this situation.

1222
01:33:54.546 --> 01:33:57.423
Min wouldn't be in this situation!

1223
01:33:58.883 --> 01:34:04.472
Look. kids. we made it
out of there safely. right?

1224
01:34:05.849 --> 01:34:10.603
And besides us. nobody knows
what happened there. Right?

1225
01:34:11.396 --> 01:34:13.982
So nothing happened. You understand?

1226
01:34:15.358 --> 01:34:19.612
I've got my own plan.

1227
01:34:20.280 --> 01:34:23.575
So you two just forget about it. okay?

1228
01:34:24.409 --> 01:34:26.953
Let's go home.

1229
01:34:27.078 --> 01:34:29.080
Let's go and take a bath.

1230
01:34:48.016 --> 01:34:50.435
What are you doing there? Hurry up!

1231
01:35:03.823 --> 01:35:06.034
What's going on?

1232
01:35:08.453 --> 01:35:11.164
You stay there.
This is all sewage water.

1233
01:35:11.289 --> 01:35:13.416
Was our window open?

1234
01:35:18.213 --> 01:35:20.840
Help me out. Ki-taek!

1235
01:35:29.390 --> 01:35:30.767
Ki-woo!

1236
01:35:33.186 --> 01:35:35.980
Hey. Ki-woo. close the window!

1237
01:35:36.648 --> 01:35:39.234
- (Electric buzz)
- You got shocked?

1238
01:35:39.359 --> 01:35:41.194
(Delirious moaning)

1239
01:35:46.157 --> 01:35:47.784
I'm dizzy.

1240
01:35:51.454 --> 01:35:55.208
Hold on a sec. Wait.

1241
01:36:00.922 --> 01:36:02.757
Shit. I'm dizzy.

1242
01:36:07.053 --> 01:36:09.138
(Ki-woo) Ki-jung. be careful!

1243
01:36:10.765 --> 01:36:12.392
Don't touch anything!

1244
01:36:15.019 --> 01:36:16.437
(Retching)

1245
01:36:24.737 --> 01:36:30.243
Honey... I've got a concussion.

1246
01:36:30.785 --> 01:36:32.745
I can't see you.

1247
01:36:54.726 --> 01:36:58.980
Honey... that woman Chung-sook...

1248
01:37:00.106 --> 01:37:01.899
Oh. God...

1249
01:37:02.025 --> 01:37:04.068
What a nice person.

1250
01:37:05.945 --> 01:37:09.073
She kicked me down the stairs.

1251
01:37:11.659 --> 01:37:13.411
Repeat after me...

1252
01:37:14.454 --> 01:37:16.581
Chung-sook...

1253
01:37:18.499 --> 01:37:21.044
'Chung-sook...'

1254
01:37:31.095 --> 01:37:33.097
Hey. Ki-woo!

1255
01:37:34.223 --> 01:37:36.851
What are you doing there? Huh?

1256
01:37:52.116 --> 01:37:55.828
H-O-L-P... M...

1257
01:39:01.477 --> 01:39:04.105
- Dad?
- Huh?

1258
01:39:05.606 --> 01:39:09.068
What was your plan?

1259
01:39:10.945 --> 01:39:12.947
What are you talking about?

1260
01:39:13.865 --> 01:39:16.993
Before. you said you had a plan.

1261
01:39:17.118 --> 01:39:20.621
What will you do
about the basement?

1262
01:39:24.250 --> 01:39:27.545
Ki-woo. you know
what kind of plan never fails?

1263
01:39:29.422 --> 01:39:31.883
No plan at all. No plan.

1264
01:39:32.008 --> 01:39:34.093
(In English) No plan.

1265
01:39:34.218 --> 01:39:36.053
You know why?

1266
01:39:37.513 --> 01:39:43.728
If you make a plan.
life never works out that way.

1267
01:39:44.896 --> 01:39:46.814
Look around us.

1268
01:39:46.939 --> 01:39:52.403
Did these people think.
"Let's all spend the night in a gym"?

1269
01:39:53.237 --> 01:39:58.826
But look now. Everyone's sleeping
on the floor. us included.

1270
01:40:00.912 --> 01:40:04.040
That's why people shouldn't make plans.

1271
01:40:06.125 --> 01:40:10.254
With no plan. nothing can go wrong.

1272
01:40:10.379 --> 01:40:16.636
And if something spins out of control.
it doesn't matter.

1273
01:40:18.054 --> 01:40:20.848
Whether you kill someone.
or betray your country.

1274
01:40:22.391 --> 01:40:26.020
None of it fucking matters. Got it?

1275
01:40:27.980 --> 01:40:29.398
Dad?

1276
01:40:31.484 --> 01:40:32.902
I'm sorry.

1277
01:40:33.736 --> 01:40:35.238
For what?

1278
01:40:38.407 --> 01:40:39.825
Everything.

1279
01:40:40.868 --> 01:40:42.495
All Of it.

1280
01:40:44.705 --> 01:40:49.043
- I'll take care of everything.
- What are you talking about?

1281
01:40:51.671 --> 01:40:54.090
Why are you hugging that stone?

1282
01:40:55.007 --> 01:40:56.425
This?

1283
01:41:02.139 --> 01:41:05.101
It keeps clinging to me.

1284
01:41:07.520 --> 01:41:11.148
I think you need some sleep.

1285
01:41:14.694 --> 01:41:16.320
I'm serious.

1286
01:41:17.989 --> 01:41:19.991
It keeps following me.

1287
01:41:24.829 --> 01:41:26.455
(Birds chirruping)

1288
01:41:32.753 --> 01:41:35.590
(Yeon-kyo) Miss Jessica.
sorry to call on Sunday morning.

1289
01:41:35.715 --> 01:41:38.050
Are you free for lunch today?

1290
01:41:38.175 --> 01:41:41.554
'We're having an impromptu birthday
for Da-song.'

1291
01:41:41.679 --> 01:41:45.099
Ah... a birthday party?

1292
01:41:45.224 --> 01:41:48.811
If you come too.
Da-song will be so happy.

1293
01:41:48.936 --> 01:41:52.773
And have as much pasta. gratin.
and salmon steak as you want.

1294
01:41:52.898 --> 01:41:57.903
Please come for 1:00pm. and
I'll count today as one of your lessons.

1295
01:41:58.029 --> 01:41:59.780
(In English) You know what I mean?

1296
01:41:59.905 --> 01:42:01.324
See you soon.

1297
01:42:02.366 --> 01:42:03.784
Mum?

1298
01:42:03.909 --> 01:42:07.538
For the party.
shouldn't we invite Kevin too?

1299
01:42:07.663 --> 01:42:10.416
Great idea! Why not?
Will you call him?

1300
01:42:10.541 --> 01:42:14.420
Get some more sleep. honey!
You must be tired after yesterday.

1301
01:42:14.545 --> 01:42:18.924
If we have a party.
won't you need to do the rounds?

1302
01:42:19.050 --> 01:42:22.887
Right. the wine shop.
supermarket. bakery. florist...

1303
01:42:23.012 --> 01:42:26.682
But I've already told Mr. Kim
to hurry over.

1304
01:42:26.807 --> 01:42:29.352
- I'll pay him overtime.
- (In English) Perfect.

1305
01:42:29.477 --> 01:42:30.895
(Humming)

1306
01:42:36.859 --> 01:42:38.277
(Shouting)

1307
01:42:39.862 --> 01:42:43.574
Everyone sit down. I'll explain!

1308
01:42:44.241 --> 01:42:49.580
DA-HYE: WE'RE HAVING A PARTY.
AND MUM SAID TO INVITE YOU

1309
01:42:51.749 --> 01:42:57.421
Sis. in the basement.
we have ten outdoor tables.

1310
01:42:57.546 --> 01:43:01.092
First take them all out.
then arrange them...

1311
01:43:02.051 --> 01:43:05.054
No. come to the window.
I need to show you.

1312
01:43:06.972 --> 01:43:12.186
With Da-song's tent in the middle.
curve the tables outward...

1313
01:43:12.728 --> 01:43:14.689
A crane's wing formation!

1314
01:43:14.814 --> 01:43:18.359
Like Admiral Yi used. you know?
At the Battle of Hansan Island!

1315
01:43:18.484 --> 01:43:20.695
Think of the tent
as the Japanese warship.

1316
01:43:20.820 --> 01:43:25.866
And our tables will make
a semi-circular crane's wing formation.

1317
01:43:25.991 --> 01:43:30.329
'Then near the tent will be
the barbeque grill. firewood and such.

1318
01:43:30.454 --> 01:43:32.123
'Arrange them all there.'

1319
01:43:32.248 --> 01:43:37.461
Ha-ha! Oh. sure.
bring your husband too! Yeah.

1320
01:43:37.586 --> 01:43:41.215
And definitely no presents.
just come.

1321
01:43:42.299 --> 01:43:47.096
What dress code? It's impromptu.
you can wear sweat pants!

1322
01:43:48.723 --> 01:43:53.978
And definitely no presents.
Just come and eat hors d'oeuvres!

1323
01:43:55.688 --> 01:43:57.648
You know my culinary skills.

1324
01:43:57.773 --> 01:44:02.278
Right! We'll just get drunk
in the daytime.

1325
01:44:04.238 --> 01:44:07.825
If you'd sing. that'd be great!
You know the one...

1326
01:44:07.950 --> 01:44:09.785
(♪ Sings Italian opera)

1327
01:44:23.841 --> 01:44:26.677
Quiet... he's sleeping.

1328
01:44:26.802 --> 01:44:30.556
Today the sky's so blue.
and there's no pollution.

1329
01:44:30.681 --> 01:44:35.060
Thanks to all the rain yesterday. Right.

1330
01:44:35.186 --> 01:44:39.023
So we traded camping
for a garden party.

1331
01:44:40.232 --> 01:44:41.859
Lemons into lemonade!

1332
01:44:43.235 --> 01:44:44.653
(Sniffs)

1333
01:44:45.237 --> 01:44:49.408
Right. that rain was such a blessing.

1334
01:44:49.533 --> 01:44:50.868
(Coughs)

1335
01:44:51.494 --> 01:44:56.081
And definitely no presents. I mean it.

1336
01:44:56.749 --> 01:45:00.961
Right. just squeeze
your Mini Cooper into the garage.

1337
01:45:01.086 --> 01:45:07.176
Go on up! Right. back it in.
Just don't block the Benz.

1338
01:45:07.301 --> 01:45:11.472
Oh. you're here! It's been so long!

1339
01:45:12.807 --> 01:45:15.309
I told you no presents...

1340
01:45:33.577 --> 01:45:35.871
You were thinking of something else.

1341
01:45:35.996 --> 01:45:38.040
(Ki-woo) Huh?

1342
01:45:38.165 --> 01:45:41.710
While kissing me.
you were thinking of something else.

1343
01:45:43.629 --> 01:45:44.839
No.

1344
01:45:45.714 --> 01:45:49.301
What do you mean?
You're doing it now. too.

1345
01:45:52.012 --> 01:45:53.305
Wow...

1346
01:45:55.057 --> 01:45:57.643
Everyone looks gorgeous. right?

1347
01:45:58.894 --> 01:46:02.606
Even for a sudden gathering.
they look so cool.

1348
01:46:03.816 --> 01:46:06.068
And so natural.

1349
01:46:07.987 --> 01:46:10.239
- Da-hye...
- Hmm?

1350
01:46:12.074 --> 01:46:13.909
Do I fit in here?

1351
01:46:15.160 --> 01:46:16.412
What?

1352
01:46:17.454 --> 01:46:20.374
In this setting. do I fit in?

1353
01:46:30.718 --> 01:46:33.012
Hey. where are you going?

1354
01:46:33.137 --> 01:46:34.847
I need to go down.

1355
01:46:34.972 --> 01:46:36.974
Just stay with me.

1356
01:46:38.183 --> 01:46:40.477
I need to go down.

1357
01:46:40.603 --> 01:46:44.940
Why go to those boring people?
Can't you stay here?

1358
01:46:46.066 --> 01:46:50.779
Not to those people... down lower.

1359
01:46:50.905 --> 01:46:53.490
Wow. what's that?

1360
01:46:56.744 --> 01:47:00.205
God. I can't believe
I'm doing this at my age.

1361
01:47:01.040 --> 01:47:02.958
It's so embarrassing.

1362
01:47:03.959 --> 01:47:05.794
I'm really sorry. Mr. Kim.

1363
01:47:05.920 --> 01:47:09.089
Da-song's mother insisted.
it can't be helped.

1364
01:47:09.214 --> 01:47:11.884
But the concept is simple.

1365
01:47:12.009 --> 01:47:16.096
There'|| be a parade
with Jessica carrying a birthday cake.

1366
01:47:16.221 --> 01:47:20.142
Then we jump out and attack Jessica.

1367
01:47:20.267 --> 01:47:23.354
- Swinging our tomahawks!
- Right.

1368
01:47:23.479 --> 01:47:28.400
Just then. Da-song the good Indian
will jump out and we'll do battle.

1369
01:47:29.276 --> 01:47:33.656
Finally. he'll save Jessica
the cake princess. and they'll all cheer.

1370
01:47:33.781 --> 01:47:37.242
Something like that.
Silly. isn't it?

1371
01:47:37.368 --> 01:47:42.373
I guess your wife likes events
and surprises.

1372
01:47:42.498 --> 01:47:44.708
Yeah. she does.

1373
01:47:44.833 --> 01:47:47.419
But she's particularly into this party.

1374
01:47:48.963 --> 01:47:51.799
You're trying your best. too.

1375
01:47:53.592 --> 01:47:55.970
Well. you love her. after all.

1376
01:48:01.475 --> 01:48:02.893
Mr. Kim...

1377
01:48:04.520 --> 01:48:07.064
You're getting paid extra.

1378
01:48:12.319 --> 01:48:16.323
Think of this as part of your work. okay?

1379
01:48:27.960 --> 01:48:30.546
- Have you been down below?
- Not yet.

1380
01:48:30.671 --> 01:48:35.342
Shouldn't we talk to them?
Reach an understanding?

1381
01:48:35.467 --> 01:48:36.635
Exactly.

1382
01:48:36.760 --> 01:48:39.346
We all got too fucking worked up
last night.

1383
01:48:39.471 --> 01:48:42.850
Dad was going on about some plan...

1384
01:48:43.726 --> 01:48:46.186
- I'm just going down there.
- Hold on.

1385
01:48:46.311 --> 01:48:48.439
Take this down to them.

1386
01:48:48.564 --> 01:48:50.190
- They must be hungry.
- Right.

1387
01:48:50.315 --> 01:48:52.109
Let them eat first.

1388
01:48:52.985 --> 01:48:56.321
Come next time for sure.

1389
01:48:56.447 --> 01:48:58.532
Here you are. Jessica.

1390
01:48:58.657 --> 01:49:01.035
- This is so amazing.
- Isn't it great?

1391
01:49:01.160 --> 01:49:03.579
I've got a special favour to ask.

1392
01:49:03.704 --> 01:49:05.164
What is it?

1393
01:49:05.289 --> 01:49:09.209
This is... How to describe it?
...Da-song's trauma recovery cake?

1394
01:49:09.334 --> 01:49:12.504
So it needs to be you who does it.
Today's highlight.

1395
01:50:23.492 --> 01:50:25.035
(Ki-woo gasps)

1396
01:50:35.629 --> 01:50:38.841
Hey. are you okay?

1397
01:50:44.221 --> 01:50:46.014
Are you...?

1398
01:50:48.934 --> 01:50:50.894
(Geun-sae screams)

1399
01:50:55.440 --> 01:50:57.151
Wait. Mister!

1400
01:51:00.696 --> 01:51:02.322
(Metallic clanging)

1401
01:51:20.507 --> 01:51:23.010
(♪ Sings Italian opera)

1402
01:51:35.063 --> 01:51:36.481
(Glass smashes)

1403
01:52:14.436 --> 01:52:16.104
Ah! Ha-ha!

1404
01:52:26.114 --> 01:52:27.950
(Laughter and applause outside)

1405
01:52:34.164 --> 01:52:35.999
(Incoherent muttering)

1406
01:52:44.091 --> 01:52:46.593
Kevin? Kevin!

1407
01:52:53.558 --> 01:52:57.604
(Yeon-kyo) Da-song. happy birthday!
Congratulations!

1408
01:52:57.729 --> 01:52:59.982
(Screaming)

1409
01:53:05.279 --> 01:53:06.405
Shit...

1410
01:53:11.034 --> 01:53:12.077
(Screaming)

1411
01:53:16.415 --> 01:53:18.375
Stop!

1412
01:53:18.500 --> 01:53:20.544
Chung-sook!

1413
01:53:20.669 --> 01:53:22.921
- (Chung-sook) Ki-jung!
- Come out here. Chung-sook!

1414
01:53:23.046 --> 01:53:26.591
Stop the blood!
Push down on the wound!

1415
01:53:31.179 --> 01:53:33.974
- Da-song!
- (Dong-ik) Honey!

1416
01:53:35.851 --> 01:53:37.686
Let go! Don't!

1417
01:53:40.230 --> 01:53:42.232
(Screaming and wailing)

1418
01:53:44.109 --> 01:53:45.819
(Ki-jung moans)

1419
01:53:48.613 --> 01:53:50.032
It hurts.

1420
01:53:55.203 --> 01:53:57.581
- The emergency room!
- (Dong-ik) Get the car!

1421
01:53:57.706 --> 01:54:01.668
- Mr. Kim! What are you doing?
- We can't wait for an ambulance!

1422
01:54:01.793 --> 01:54:06.923
Stop pushing. Dad.
It makes it hurt more.

1423
01:54:07.883 --> 01:54:11.553
Car keys! Car keys!
Throw them! Throw me the keys!

1424
01:54:19.186 --> 01:54:20.729
(Screaming)

1425
01:54:29.613 --> 01:54:32.949
- Ki-jung!
- Don't touch it...

1426
01:54:35.410 --> 01:54:37.829
Hello. Mr. Park.

1427
01:54:37.954 --> 01:54:40.582
- You know me?
- (In English) Respect!

1428
01:54:43.585 --> 01:54:44.836
(Groans)

1429
01:55:01.520 --> 01:55:02.938
(Screaming)

1430
01:56:05.584 --> 01:56:07.377
(Muffled laughter)

1431
01:56:07.502 --> 01:56:10.088
(Ki-woo) 'Opening my eyes
for the first time in a month.

1432
01:56:10.213 --> 01:56:12.883
'I saw a detective...'

1433
01:56:13.008 --> 01:56:17.637
You have the right to an attorney...

1434
01:56:17.762 --> 01:56:20.182
(Ki-woo) '...who looked nothing
like a detective.'

1435
01:56:20.307 --> 01:56:22.142
(Ki-woo giggles)

1436
01:56:24.394 --> 01:56:26.313
Is he laughing?

1437
01:56:26.438 --> 01:56:28.064
Just a second.

1438
01:56:28.523 --> 01:56:33.153
(Ki-woo) 'Then the doctor who looked
nothing like a doctor spoke.'

1439
01:56:34.404 --> 01:56:38.116
That happens sometimes
after brain surgery.

1440
01:56:38.241 --> 01:56:40.243
They keep laughing for no reason.

1441
01:56:41.119 --> 01:56:44.706
Do you hear me? Can you hear me?

1442
01:56:45.624 --> 01:56:48.293
- Then do I have to do it again?
- Do what?

1443
01:56:48.418 --> 01:56:50.420
Read him his rights.

1444
01:56:52.172 --> 01:56:55.008
- You have the right to remain silent.
- (Laughs)

1445
01:56:55.133 --> 01:56:59.095
Anything you say can and will
be used against you...

1446
01:56:59.221 --> 01:57:01.306
He keeps laughing. look!

1447
01:57:04.643 --> 01:57:10.482
(Ki-woo) 'Even when I heard
how much Ki-jung bled that day...'

1448
01:57:10.607 --> 01:57:12.943
(Judge addresses court)

1449
01:57:13.068 --> 01:57:20.200
'Even when I heard the words forgery.
trespass. foul play. self-defence.

1450
01:57:20.325 --> 01:57:24.496
'and we were lucky to get away
with a suspended sentence...

1451
01:57:27.791 --> 01:57:31.002
'Even when I finally got to see
Ki-jung's face...'

1452
01:57:31.127 --> 01:57:33.672
KIM KI-JUNG. RIP

1453
01:57:35.382 --> 01:57:37.676
'...I kept laughing.

1454
01:57:47.477 --> 01:57:52.899
'Still. when I went back
and watched the news reports.

1455
01:57:53.024 --> 01:57:55.151
'I didn't laugh.'

1456
01:57:55.277 --> 01:57:58.321
(TV Reporter) 'This sudden rampage
in the backyard of an upper-class home

1457
01:57:58.446 --> 01:58:00.240
'is a highly unusual case.

1458
01:58:00.365 --> 01:58:04.661
'Since the homeless man who sparked
the rampage died at the scene.

1459
01:58:04.786 --> 01:58:10.041
'police are struggling
to even establish a clear motive.'

1460
01:58:10.166 --> 01:58:14.671
'The driver Kim and the slain Mr. Park
are said to have been on good terms.

1461
01:58:14.796 --> 01:58:19.759
'For now. the police investigation
is focused on locating the driver Kim.'

1462
01:58:20.677 --> 01:58:24.556
'After exiting this door
and descending the stairs.

1463
01:58:24.681 --> 01:58:28.560
'Kim disappeared
into the neighbouring alleys.

1464
01:58:28.685 --> 01:58:34.024
'Police searched the CCTV footage
of nearby homes to no avail.

1465
01:58:34.149 --> 01:58:37.694
'and they have yet to find
any witnesses.

1466
01:58:37.819 --> 01:58:40.071
'Given the situation.

1467
01:58:40.196 --> 01:58:45.160
'it's not an exaggeration to say
that Kim has vanished into thin air.'

1468
01:58:46.620 --> 01:58:53.460
(Ki-woo) 'Actually. mum and I had
no idea where Dad was.'

1469
01:58:53.585 --> 01:58:55.587
(Clattering)

1470
01:58:55.712 --> 01:59:01.217
'But those detectives still
wore themselves out tailing us.

1471
01:59:05.347 --> 01:59:08.975
'Eventually the news went quiet.

1472
01:59:09.100 --> 01:59:11.811
'And after the tails stopped.

1473
01:59:11.936 --> 01:59:15.106
'I started going up that mountain.

1474
01:59:17.484 --> 01:59:21.821
'From up there.
you get a great view of the house.

1475
01:59:25.033 --> 01:59:31.539
'That clay. despite the cold.
I felt like staying longer.'

1476
01:59:45.387 --> 01:59:48.056
Dash-dash-dot-dot...

1477
01:59:52.894 --> 01:59:56.898
Dot-dot-dot-dash. dash-dash-dot...

1478
01:59:57.774 --> 01:59:59.776
(Continues muttering Morse Code)

1479
02:00:14.040 --> 02:00:15.458
"Son"!

1480
02:00:17.377 --> 02:00:19.212
(Ki-taek) 'Son...

1481
02:00:20.922 --> 02:00:24.759
'Perhaps you. if no one else.
will be able to read this letter.

1482
02:00:28.012 --> 02:00:33.935
'You were a Boy Scout.
so I'm writing this just in case.

1483
02:00:37.647 --> 02:00:40.275
'Have your injuries healed?

1484
02:00:41.484 --> 02:00:45.488
'I'm sure your mother
is plenty healthy.

1485
02:00:49.701 --> 02:00:52.245
'I'm doing fine in here.

1486
02:00:53.621 --> 02:00:56.249
'Though thinking of Ki-jung
makes me cry.

1487
02:00:59.627 --> 02:01:03.923
'Even now. what happened that day
doesn't seem real.

1488
02:01:05.633 --> 02:01:08.595
'It feels like a dream...

1489
02:01:08.720 --> 02:01:10.555
'And yet. it doesn't.

1490
02:01:11.973 --> 02:01:16.352
'That day. as I went out the gate.
I suddenly knew...

1491
02:01:17.687 --> 02:01:19.856
'...where I needed to go.'

1492
02:01:27.238 --> 02:01:29.073
(Sirens wailing)

1493
02:01:50.136 --> 02:01:51.638
(Sighs heavily)

1494
02:01:55.016 --> 02:01:56.434
(Weeps)

1495
02:01:59.145 --> 02:02:02.065
(Ki-taek) 'A house where
such a grisly crime took place

1496
02:02:02.190 --> 02:02:05.151
'would surely not be easy to sell.'

1497
02:02:07.153 --> 02:02:08.571
(Sobbing)

1498
02:02:08.696 --> 02:02:11.157
I'm sorry. Mr. Park.

1499
02:02:11.282 --> 02:02:17.038
'I struggled to hold out like that
in an empty house.

1500
02:02:20.124 --> 02:02:23.253
'Still. thanks to the house
being empty...

1501
02:02:23.378 --> 02:02:28.132
'What was her name? Moon-gwang?

1502
02:02:28.258 --> 02:02:32.053
'I was able to give her
a proper send-off.

1503
02:02:33.721 --> 02:02:36.808
'I hear tree-side burials are very trendy.

1504
02:02:36.933 --> 02:02:39.435
'so. hell. I did my best.

1505
02:02:43.606 --> 02:02:47.193
'But those real estate sharks
sure are clever.'

1506
02:02:47.318 --> 02:02:48.945
(Muffled voices)

1507
02:02:51.948 --> 02:02:56.244
'They'd hoodwinked some people
who'd just arrived in Korea

1508
02:02:56.369 --> 02:02:58.621
'and managed to sell them the house.

1509
02:02:59.873 --> 02:03:03.167
'With the parents working
and the kids attending school.

1510
02:03:03.293 --> 02:03:05.837
'the family's usually out.

1511
02:03:05.962 --> 02:03:11.384
'But the goddamned housekeeper
stays there 24 hours a day.

1512
02:03:11.509 --> 02:03:16.180
'Each time I go upstairs.
I take my life in my hands.

1513
02:03:18.975 --> 02:03:23.605
'It turns out Germans eat more
than just sausage and beer.

1514
02:03:23.730 --> 02:03:25.857
'What a relief.

1515
02:03:28.484 --> 02:03:32.530
'Passing the time down here.
everything starts to go hazy.

1516
02:03:37.160 --> 02:03:41.039
'Today. at least I was able
to write you a letter.

1517
02:03:43.166 --> 02:03:47.045
'If I send out the letter this way
every night.

1518
02:03:47.170 --> 02:03:51.007
'maybe someday you'll see it.

1519
02:03:57.347 --> 02:03:59.390
'So long.'

1520
02:04:13.112 --> 02:04:15.531
- (Chung-sook) You're home. Ki-woo?
- Yeah.

1521
02:04:29.837 --> 02:04:34.342
(Ki-woo) 'Dad... today I made a plan.

1522
02:04:36.177 --> 02:04:38.179
'A fundamental plan.

1523
02:04:41.182 --> 02:04:44.894
'I'm going to earn money.
A lot of it.'

1524
02:04:45.019 --> 02:04:47.105
(Estate agent speaking)

1525
02:04:49.148 --> 02:04:53.569
(Ki-woo) 'University. a career. marriage.
those are all fine.

1526
02:04:53.695 --> 02:04:55.738
'but first I'll earn money.'

1527
02:04:55.863 --> 02:05:00.910
You'll see once you go in.
it's very spacious.

1528
02:05:01.619 --> 02:05:06.541
Actually. we don't show this house
to just anyone.

1529
02:05:06.666 --> 02:05:11.754
(Ki-woo) 'When I have money.
I'll buy that house.

1530
02:05:11.879 --> 02:05:16.676
'On the day we move in.
mum and I will be in the yard.

1531
02:05:16.801 --> 02:05:19.220
'Because the sunshine is so nice there.

1532
02:05:20.638 --> 02:05:24.642
'All you'll need to do
is walk up the stairs.'

1533
02:06:48.518 --> 02:06:52.146
(Ki-woo) 'Until then. take care.

1534
02:06:57.235 --> 02:06:58.986
'So long.'

1534
02:06:59.305 --> 02:07:59.457
